        # C429-1b: this is now a PER-CLASS budget, not a pool to be divided.
        # At 30, crypto received 29 and every other desk shared 1. C417 already
        # ruled that classes must not compete for slots; the Step-3 budget was
        # the last place they still did.
        self.TOP_PAIRS_SELECT = 60
        self.C429_PER_CLASS_SELECT = True   # each desk gets its own Step-3 budget
        # ═══ C429-2 IS STAGED, NOT LIVE, AND THE REASON IS A REAL QUESTION ═══
        # The infrastructure is built and VERIFIED: the ledger lock (C429-0),
        # the deferred-log filter, the entry pool and the post-Step-3 drain all
        # execute correctly. What is NOT resolved is a SEMANTIC choice that
        # belongs to the operator, not to me.
        # Today Step 5 RANKS every viable candidate and allocates margin across
        # them, so the BEST-RANKED trade gets capital first. Firing an entry the
        # moment a pair clears Step 3 replaces that with FIRST-VIABLE-WINS: the
        # pair that happens to be scored earliest takes the margin, and a better
