            ("C165", "Fixed N51 real-CVD silent failure (method was in OrderFlowAnalyzer but quick_scan in TechnicalAnalysis called self._fetch_real_cvd → AttributeError caught silently since C158 — moved to correct class); added timestamps to the file log."),

            ("C166", "Added real-CVD observability logging on viable candidates (verifies N51 is live post-C165 fix); measured true session cadence ~5.7min via new timestamps."),

            ("C167", "Graduated RSI brake — C151 used hard cliffs (full penalty at 78/22, zero just inside); now ramps from the approach to the extreme (long>70/short<30) so fading a stretched RSI costs conviction proportionally. EPIC short at RSI=27 got no brake in C166 and lost -$0.98."),
            ("C168", "Fixed misplaced ATR projection-floor: it was nested in the else-branch (fewer-than-14-candles fallback), so for ALL normal pairs the floor never applied and projected_move stayed as raw short_term×2 — rounding to +0.0% for momentum-neutral pairs (FIDA entered LONG at Proj +0.0% in C167). Floor now runs for every pair; projections reflect ATR-implied movement. Root cause of weak predicting power."),

            ("C169", "Full microscopic+macroscopic audit for live template. Quarantine-marked the dead 1,258-line full_analysis (never called; repeated bug-magnet). Wired 6 orphaned chart-pattern signals (catalyst/capitulation/double/flag/breakout/volume_trend) into _scores — they were computed and displayed but never scored. Verified all 39+6 components reach the decision; 0 unguarded iterations; data-flow integrity confirmed."),

            ("C170", "Stagnant-exit timer now keyed off the WEAKER of agreement AND score-magnitude. BEAT/TIA/FIDA all lost STAGNANT with HIGH agreement (69-87%) but MARGINAL score (0.43-0.53) — high agreement on a weak-magnitude signal drifts with no momentum, yet the C144 timer gave it 20-30min patience. Now a weak-score entry is cut in ~12min regardless of agreement. Stores pos._entry_score."),

            ("C196", "RELATIVISTIC VOLUME NORMALIZATION (C195 follow-up, now that log_c195 confirmed new-listing movers surface and get scored). Phase-2 scanner liveliness used vol_ratio = vol / max_vol where max_vol is BTC ~$3.8B 24h volume, so EVERY alt scored ~0 on the 0.40 volume + 0.35 freshness terms (75% of the ranking weight dead for alts) and pairs were ordered almost purely on raw 24h % via the 0.25 change term -- an absolute, BTC-anchored scale that violates Principle 1 (relativistic, not absolute). FIX: min-max over LOG volume across the live cohort -- _vol_ratio_s1 = (log1p(vol) - log1p_min) / (log1p_max - log1p_min) -- so pairs are ranked by ORDER OF MAGNITUDE of volume within the actual scanned set; a $5-50M mover now lands ~0.2-0.5 (was ~0.001) and its volume + freshness terms contribute, while BTC still tops out at 1.0. The 0.40/0.25/0.35 weights and the Phase-3 projected_boost (ADDED for the top-38) are untouched; net effect is the top-38 buffer fills with cohort-relative LIVELY pairs rather than only the most volatile, so genuinely active mid-caps reach full analysis. Shipped AFTER C195 (one variable at a time) -- log_c195 showed US/SYN/ORDI/ESPORTS all reaching full scoring, so visibility is proven before changing the ranking scale. NOTE: changes WHICH pairs reach deep analysis, not the entry gates -- exhaustion/RR/climax vetoes are unchanged."),
            ("C258", "EPC SUBSTANTIVE-PEAK FLOOR + CLOSING LATCH (log_c254). (a) EARLY_PEAK_CAPTURE trigger-1 (30%%-of-peak) now ALSO requires the peak itself to have cleared 0.75x the pair's OWN leveraged ATR -- the exact C251 standard extended to the third family member. Chart-proof: TLM#1 peaked +2.0%% = 0.61x its 3.28%% ATR (sub-noise crest) and trigger-1 banked it at +0.64%% on a 1.2%% intra-candle wiggle (raw give 0.37 PRU -- clearing the C246 floor by 0.02) -- the NEXT candle ran +6%% and the bot paid a 13-min gap + double fees to reboard its own move via TLM#2. Trigger-2 (0.5 PRU raw give) untouched: deep givebacks from ANY peak still bank. Retro: TLM#1 rides (0.61<0.75) and merges into the +3.9%% continuation; TLM#2 still exits (peak 1.19xATR >= 0.75); EIGEN (4.4%% run) and the ZEC class unchanged. (b) _closing latch: the 1s monitoring thread AND the main loop's pause-time monitor both evaluated TLM at 22:38:14 -- same EXIT SIGNAL logged twice, duplicate close attempt caught only by the C145 post-facto guard ('Double-close prevented' at :15). First evaluator to set pos._closing owns the close; every other evaluator skips the position -- the duplicate dies at the source, before the log and before any (in live: real) reduce-only order."),
            ("C257", "TRUE PnL ACCOUNTING -- two flattery bugs, verified to the cent (log_c254 TLM#2: booked +$0.51, true +$0.48). (a) gross_pnl used EXIT notional (size x exit_price): every win inflated by (1+move), every loss flattered by (1-move) -- reconstruction: 9018 units x 0.001778 x 3.19%% - maker-maker fees = $0.5055 = the printed $0.51 EXACTLY; correct entry-notional gross 15.54 x 3.19%% - real fees = $0.483. (b) the exit fee read pos.is_limit_order -- the ENTRY's order type -- so every monitor/sweep exit after a limit entry was billed MAKER 0.02%% instead of TAKER 0.06%% (all closes in this path are market reduce_only): fees understated 3x on most exits. Same entry-notional fix applied to get_unrealized_pnl (its gross used CURRENT notional -- unrealized gains grew quadratically with the move). Combined drift: paper equity systematically above truth -> targets fire early, Kelly sizes off phantom capital, the learning ledger records rosier trades than happened, and live results would mysteriously underperform paper. ~+4.6%% per-win inflation compounding across every trade since the accounting was written. Fee display now 3dp (was printing 'Entry $0.00 + Exit $0.00 = $0.01')."),
            ("C256", "OVERSHOOT LEDGER RETIRED -- user spec, deliberately reversing C178/C204. Targets are now the plain schedule: Normal-1 1.00%% / HP-1 0.75%% / Normal-2 0.50%% / HP-2 0.25%%, each of THAT phase's own start equity, and every phase's start equity = the previous phase's MARKED ending equity (C255). Overshoot therefore carries forward AS EQUITY -- the next phase starts higher and its full %% is demanded on top -- so a credit ledger double-serves the same purpose while adding failure surface: log_c254 shows the skip machinery, fed by the cash/marked anchor split, 'achieving' HP-1 in 15 seconds with zero HP trades, skipping HP-2, and completing a 4-phase session in 31 seconds off ONE open position's unrealized mark -- then pausing the bot out of that same position's +8.8%% continuation (TLM 0.001778 -> 0.001934 within 1.6h of the phantom completion; ~$1.4 of runner continuation forfeited on the $15.54 margin). effective_cycle_target now returns (base, base); settle_cycle_overshoot logs the carry informationally and pins the credit to 0 (persistence-compatible); _advance_session_phase ALWAYS advances -- a session is exactly four traded phases. The C178 'converge to ~2.5%%/day' goal is preserved BY CONSTRUCTION: 1.00+0.75+0.50+0.25 on cascading start equities."),
            ("C255", "MODE-EQUITY UNIFICATION -- the session's headline bug (log_c254: 4-phase session completed in 31 seconds, 22:32:20->22:32:51). Achievement checks used MARKED equity (get_live_equity = cash + unrealized) but every phase-boundary anchor stored CASH-ONLY portfolio.equity: Normal-1 achieved at live $50.58 while HP start was snapshotted $50.12 -- so the open TLM runner's $0.41 unrealized was instantly re-counted as HP-1's entire 'gain' (0.82%% in 15s, zero HP trades), AGAIN as Normal-2's (0.88%% in 16s), and the stale $50.12 was frozen as 'Session end equity' and next-day baseline while the runner later realized +$0.51 -- tomorrow's Normal-1 would have started ~1%% pre-achieved for free, compounding daily. ONE unit everywhere now: (a) the Normal- and HP-branch transitions pass get_live_equity recomputed AFTER the sweep (realized sweep PnL + the spared runner's live mark both included); (b) revert_to_normal anchors marked; (c) the session-resume path re-anchors to live equity AS OF RESUME (next_day_equity kept only as the exchange-hiccup fallback) -- positions can close during the pause, so the pause-moment snapshot is stale by construction. Retro on the real sequence: HP-1 starts at $50.58 marked, reads -0.1%% fifteen seconds later -> NO phantom achievement; the session stays live through TLM's +8.8%% evening leg instead of pausing at 22:32. Runner-mode interaction note: C242 runners now make an open position AT every boundary the COMMON case -- marked anchoring is not an edge-case nicety, it is the only correct accounting."),
            ("C254", "CASCADE-COHERENCE RELEASE for the C240 short gate -- the C243<->C240 doctrine conflict, resolved (log_c248 directional tally: 46 long vs 12 short final candidates, ZERO shorts entered all session while THE fell -15.2%%, TLM -16.7%%, SLX -15.9%% exactly as their own flow vetoes/scores flagged; DYDX short 0.960 and VELVET short 0.716 blocked as 'parabola_bounce' 1.7-2.2 ATR off lows that were being REMADE -- +7.2%% and +10.5%% with zero adverse, chart-verified). C243 was built to enable cascade shorts by halving the RSI brake when its trio confirms (flow vote aligned >=0.35 + oi_div aligned >=0.20 + shorts NOT crowded); forty lines later C240 hard-blocked the same trades because in a live cascade the day-low is never 'fresh' -- the distance-from-extreme test measures staleness of a low that is not stale, it is falling. FIX: in the C240 SHORT branch only, release iff _rsv244 (C244 resolution, unchanged) OR _brake_mult<1.0 (the C243 trio) -- same x0.85 score / x0.925 conf penalty, distinct wave log. The trio is already computed unconditionally in the same scope (zero new fetches); long side untouched (long-block chart-vindicated on TAIKO/BAS/M repeatedly). HONEST retro note: this session's DYDX read CVD +0.02..+0.18 (covering, not fresh money) and likely would NOT have confirmed -- C254 does not claim that miss; it removes the architectural contradiction so future CONFIRMED cascades (the C243 DYDX-class with OI rising into the break) are reachable at all."),
            ("C253", "THE PHANTOM _atr_pct -- a one-character naming mismatch that silently disabled the entire relativistic exit family (grep-proof: the Position dataclass field is atr_pct, populated at creation; EIGHT consumers read getattr(pos,'_atr_pct',0.5) WITH underscore -- never assigned anywhere -- so the C241 trailing-TP allowance, the C241 PEAK_REVERSAL noise veto, the C242 runner-selection window in BOTH Normal and HP target blocks, the DRI-threshold ATR modulation, the C170 stagnation ATR scaling and the C87 GARCH ratio ALL ran on the hardcoded 0.5%% default for every pair every session since C241 shipped. log_c248 chart-proof: TAIKO#1's trailing allowance printed 0.70%% = 1.25x0.5xlev EXACTLY on a pair breathing 2-3%% per candle -> premature TP at +2.0%% -> the 02:32 re-chase -> -$0.37; C242's runner window collapsed to 0.25%% of price -> zero runners qualified in any log since C242 shipped; ALLO/TAIKO allowances printed near-identical 0.6-0.7 on pairs with 3x different vol -- the constant was the tell). FIX (3 parts): (a) _open_position sets pos._atr_pct from the SAME floored TR-ATR the PRU uses -- one unit for PRU and every trail; (b) monitor's DRI block EWMA-refreshes it from settled candles (14-bar true-range, alpha=0.25, floor 0.30) so the trail breathes with live vol expansion; (c) persisted in save_state/load (Atlas #23: every getattr default is a silent liar until the attribute provably exists -- reloaded positions would have resurrected the phantom). Golden Rule executed: all 8 read-sites audited against the one write-site."),
            ("C252", "RE-ENTRY CHASE MEMORY + C88-H2 REVIVAL -- two phantoms, one store (log_c248: TAIKO exited TRAILING_TP +2.0%% at 02:20 IST and was re-entered SAME direction 12min later at +3.9%% ABOVE the bot's own exit price = +1.6 of the pair's OWN ATR of adverse displacement, straight into the chart-verified spike top -> -$0.37 STAGNANT_LOSS; meanwhile FARTCOIN's re-entry 147min after its profitable exit WON +$0.15 -- time had reset the structure. Root cause: the bot kept NO memory of where it got off; worse, C88's Heuristic-2 believed it did -- it read self._closed_positions_tracker which was NEVER CREATED anywhere (phantom-attribute class, C253's sibling): the same-pair-loss bar-raise has been dead code since C88). FIX: (a) _close_position_inner writes self._recent_exits[symbol]={side,px,ts,pnl,pnl_pct,atr} (atr snapshotted from the now-real C253 value; dict trimmed to 12 by age); (b) Step-3 gate after C240: same pair + same dir + PROFITABLE exit < 45min ago + price already >0.5xATR BEYOND the exit price in the trade direction -> BLOCK 'reentry_chase' (boomerang log, best_rejected updated) -- paying up for the move already sold; loss exits are NOT hard-gated (orthogonality) and better-priced re-entries pass; (c) C88-H2 rewired to the real store: same-pair LOSS <1h ago -> bar x1.25 (now actually fires). Retro: TAIKO#2 blocked at 1.6 ATR (-$0.37 saved), FARTCOIN#2 passes on age (8820s), first entries of any pair untouched."),
            ("C251", "PEAK_FLOOR NOISE VETO -- fourth member of the C241 family (log_c248 first-hour massacre: LAB long peaked +1.1%% = 0.7 PRU thirteen minutes in, wiggled to -0.2%% -- a 1.3%% round-trip INSIDE the pair's own candle breathing -- the C98 breakeven backstop fired 'profit fully erased', and LAB then rallied +15.6%% chart-verified; with BEAT and RE killed the same hour by the same class of sub-noise reads, the session's three best entries -- scores 0.61-0.72, the only FEEDBACK-CONFIRM entry of the night among them -- returned -$0.28 while their pairs ran +8/+11/+16%%: ~$3.5-5 of forfeited moves). C241 fixed this disease for TRAILING_TP and PEAK_REVERSAL, C246 for EARLY_PEAK_CAPTURE; the breakeven backstop was deliberately left raw and log_c248 is the proof it is the same illness: a 'peak' that never cleared the pair's own noise band is not a crest, it is a flutter -- erasing it is not reversal, it is the same flutter. FIX: PEAK_FLOOR (pnl<=0 AND peak>0.6 PRU) now fires ONLY if the peak itself was substantive: peak_pnl_pct >= 0.75 x the pair's OWN leveraged ATR (the C241 unit, real post-C253) OR peak >= 1.0 PRU (deep by definition -- the LUNA class still exits at breakeven). Sub-noise peaks fall through to the DRI / stagnant / REL_HARD_STOP floors that bound the downside exactly as before. Retro: LAB survives (peak 1.1%% < 0.75x1.8%%-lev, 0.7<1.0 PRU) -> rides to the C241 trail; LUNA-class (1.0 PRU peaks) fires unchanged."),
            ("C250", "C92 LIVE RESULTANT -- WICK-PROOFING THE REGIME EXIT, three locks (log_c248 22:00:27 IST: 'C92 RESULTANT FLIP: scan=+0.09 -> live=-0.57' fired off ONE intracandle BTC wick to 61,106 -- the 16:00 UTC candle's LOW, which settled ABOVE it and fully recovered by 17:00, chart-verified -- and the REGIME_EXIT flushed BEAT at -0.1%% and RE at -0.8%% seventeen seconds after latching; both rallied +8.2%%/+10.9%%. Anatomy of the false kill: (1) returns anchored on _btc_c[-1], the FORMING candle's live tick -- Atlas 0b violation, a wick that never settles spoke for the regime; (2) tanh((ret_1h/ref_atr)x0.5) SATURATES at |z|>~1.5, so in a quiet tape (ref_atr 0.10-0.15%%) any +/-0.4%% hourly wiggle read as +/-0.9 -- the h1 term was a sign detector, not a measurement; (3) the exit gate demanded only _pnl_in_pru<0 -- ANY epsilon-red tick -- with zero persistence and zero consultation of the position's own reversal metric: the DENT disease reborn at macro level). FIX -- four locks, each validated on the REAL settled-candle table of the false-kill afternoon (14:00-19:30 UTC fetched live from Bitget): (a) settled closes -- now=c[-2], 1h vs c[-6], 4h vs c[-18] (Atlas 0b); (b) sqrt-time normalization -- h1's divisor ref_atr -> 2x ref_atr (a 1h return spans 4 candles; its random-walk unit is sqrt(4)x the 15m ATR; the 1x divisor made |h1|>=0.9 on 9 of 23 settled rows of a FLAT afternoon -- a sign detector, not a measurement; h4's 3x kept, ~sqrt16-scaled); (c) Ornstein-Uhlenbeck low-pass: R_s = lam*R_s + (1-lam)*R_raw, lam=exp(-dt/240s) -- one-tick spikes decay as e^(-t/tau), consumers see R_s; (d) lock-0 h4-AUTHORITY on the flip itself: the regime is MACROSCOPIC, so a flip claim additionally requires the settled 4h term to oppose the scan (|h4|>0.20 against) -- at the kill read the blend was -0.44 but its decomposition was 0.4x(-0.89 saturated h1) + 0.6x(-0.13 h4): the macroscopic term NEVER confirmed and BTC recovered within 2 candles; plus the arming clock (>=90s persistence), materiality (position losing >=0.25 of its OWN PRU -- epsilon-red is not evidence), and the position's own smoothed DRI veto (<-0.05 -- pair-level truth outranks market-level inference for a position already on the books). Retro on the REAL sequence with honest timing math: at the actual 22:00:27 kill instant the EWMA still reads ~+0.29 (settled raw had been POSITIVE +0.31 until that candle) -> no flip -> BEAT and RE both survive the actual kill outright; the settled raw then dips to -0.44 for exactly ONE candle, whose EWMA crossing would have opened a residual 16:36-16:48 UTC window -- the h4-authority lock (h4=-0.13, never past -0.20 anywhere in the 5.5h table) removes that window entirely: ZERO flips fire in the whole afternoon; a REAL regime break (h4 walking through -0.20 over hours, as in the 14:00 trend rollover) still flips -- slower is CORRECT for a regime claim, REL_HARD_STOP and the DRI hard exit own the fast lane. BEAT's materiality lock is independently verified (-0.1%%/PRU 2.63 = -0.04 PRU >> -0.25). The C126-F49 scan-level REGIME_EXIT block is untouched (didn't fire this session)."),
            ("C249", "SESSION-COUPLING ENTRY FLOOR -- first delivered slice of the Atlas 8 macro module (measured foundation: BTC<->NDX 1h-return correlation +0.55..+0.67 during US hours 19:00-01:30 IST vs +0.06 in the Asia dead-zone -- the tape's information content is session-dependent, and the correlation itself is regime-dependent so it is interpolated, never hardcoded). log_c248 ledger by IST entry hour: ALL three sub-0.60-score entries of the night came in the 02:00-07:30 dead-zone and ALL lost (TAIKO#2 0.576 -$0.37 chase, SLX 0.462 -$0.12 longed into the -16%% its own absorption veto had flagged, M 0.506 -$0.37 hard-stopped at the exact wick low ~= -$0.86 total), while every dead-zone WINNER scored >=0.63 -- score quality separates cleanly at the floor this fix draws. NOT a curfew: a genuinely strong signal still trades at 04:00; the floor demands MORE conviction exactly when the tape carries LESS information. Mechanics: w(h_IST) = C1 cosine interpolation through anchors (1.5,1.0)->(4.0,0.15)->(9.0,0.15)->(13.5,0.55)->(19.0,1.0)->(25.5,1.0) (h<1.5 wraps +24); if w<0.95: _eff_min_score x= 1+0.25x(1-w) -> deep-Asia 0.42->0.509 / 0.45->0.546, EU ramp ~0.50, US hours untouched; the 0.25 coefficient is LOG-MEASURED, not assumed -- the session's rejection prints reveal the operative floors (strict quality floor 0.42; other longs faced 0.48 at the SLX scan and 0.63-0.69 at the M scan) and 0.25 is the smallest coefficient that blocks BOTH sub-0.53 dead-zone losers from even the minimal 0.42 base (0.42x1.2125=0.509>0.506>0.42x1.1075=0.465>0.462) while every dead-zone winner (>=0.626 vs floors <=0.48x1.2125=0.582) clears by >=0.04; downstream 0.72 cap still bounds stacking with C88 H1/H2 (paralysis-proof); fail-open; one clock log per scan keyed to _total_scan_count (the near-phantom _scan_count at another site is noted for a future audit). Retro on all 12 entries with REAL logged scores: blocks SLX 0.462 and M 0.506 (+$0.49 saved); TAIKO#2 0.576 at h=2.54 (lift x1.079, floor <=0.50) passes HERE but C252 blocks it (defense-in-depth, each fix carries its own kill); passes BOTH FARTCOIN wins, TAIKO#1 win, ALLO win, BIRB (whose exit saved -17.8%%), and MAGMA (00:03 IST w=1.0 -- the C190 blow-off class stays deliberately unfiltered, the hard stop managed it). Deliberately NOT shipped after retro-validation: a Normal-mode feedback gate (conv<0 AND vol_trend<=-0.5) -- once C249+C252 land its only remaining retro effect was blocking TAIKO#1's +$0.09 WIN; documented in the Atlas as rejected-by-evidence."),
            ("C248", "C143 SOFT COUNTER-TREND WAIVER under C101 -- single-agency coherence completing C245 (log_c246: all 4 shorts the C245 exemption allowed through the resultant hard-block -- LIT/EPIC/BREV/ENA -- were immediately re-taxed 17-19%% by the C143 soft counter-trend penalty keyed on the BLEND bias (+0.33..+0.38), a SECOND counter-trend tax on trades the bot itself declared with-prediction). When _blow_off_top+short (or _blow_off_bottom+long), the C143 soft band is waived with a compact log; the C245 20%% is paid once. Quality/score bars untouched -- chart truth vindicated them this session (EPIC short -2.5%% at 1h, ENA -0.9%%, IN -3.1%%; only BREV +14.3 MFE was a real miss and its PRE-penalty score 0.43 was already under the 0.51 bar, so the stack changed nothing). Zero retro behaviour change -- pure logical coherence."),
            ("C247", "C101 LATCH FALSIFICATION -- the stateless 'reversal imminent' flag becomes a testable forecast (log_c246 + log_c243: C101 latched R +0.73..+0.82 / L/S 2.4-2.5 across TWO sessions, blanket-blocking 23-29 longs EVERY scan; chart truth for session 2: the market ROSE for 4+ hours after the latch -- BIRB +14.97%% MFE, XRP +3.4, ADA +2.8, AAVE +2.9, BTC +1.5 -- ALL blocked longs; the session's only trade, WLD long +5.5%% MFE, slipped through a 6-minute unlatch window at 16:20 when R dipped to +0.62). A forecast of IMMINENT reversal that persists >=2h while the market RISES is falsified, yet the flag re-latched every cycle with no memory. FIX (stateful, relativistic, graduated -- no new hard gate per the C245 lesson): the TF-vector loop stashes BTC's live close + own 15m ATR%% (same fetch, zero new requests); on latch, record start-ts + BTC reference; each cycle compute age and BTC's rise from the reference in BTC's OWN ATR units; age>=2.0h AND rise>=3.0 ATR -> latch marked STALE (warning gains a [STALE] tag). The Step-3 gate then downgrades the blanket long-block to score x0.75 / conf x0.85 with a '🔓 ... blow-off STALE (latched X.Xh, BTC +Y.Y ATR since)' log. Mirror for capitulation-bottom (fall>=3 ATR below reference -> shorts penalized not blocked). An unlatch clears the clock -- a fresh latch is a fresh forecast with full 2h blocking authority; C245's short exemption persists in the STALE state (crowd-long risk is real), so both sides trade on quality once the thesis goes stale. Retro-validated on live BTC candles: session-1 latch (09:33, market fell -- VELVET -27 etc.) NEVER goes stale (rise stays negative) -> identical behaviour, the correct block held; session-2 latch would mark STALE in the evening as BTC ground higher -> the 19:00-01:30 IST US-hours longs (ADA conv 1.00 breadth 6/6, NEAR 0.68, LINK...) become reachable at a 25%% penalty exactly when the +2-15%% moves ran."),
            ("C246", "EARLY_PEAK_CAPTURE NOISE FLOOR -- third member of the C241 family (log_c243: ZEC, the session's only trade, banked +0.7% via the %%-of-peak trigger at a 0.2-PRU giveback -- 31%% of a shallow 0.7-PRU peak is ONE candle of noise in the pair's own ATR_lev; SYN yesterday proved the class costs continuation). The percentage trigger had NO absolute floor for shallow peaks. FIX: trigger-1 (gave >=30%% of peak) now ALSO requires raw giveback >=0.35 PRU -- the same relativistic unit trigger-2 (0.5 PRU) already uses. Genuine reversals (EIGEN 33%% of a 4.4%% run) clear 0.35 PRU trivially; only the sub-noise shakeout class is vetoed. PEAK_FLOOR breakeven backstop untouched. Retro: ZEC 0.2<0.35 held through the wiggle, exits on the real fade ~+1.0-1.1%% instead of +0.7%%."),
            ("C245", "BLOW-OFF / RESULTANT COHERENCE -- the session-killing deadlock (log_c243: 1 trade in 2.5h, then 2h20m starvation while C101 latched BLOW-OFF TOP every ~5min: R +0.74..+0.82, BTC L/S 2.5, 93 'longs BLOCKED' warnings -- and the resultant gate simultaneously hard-blocked every SHORT at |R|>=0.50 as counter-trend. The two market-level gates key on the SAME R and issued opposite orders: C101 predicted 'R is terminal, reversal imminent' while the resultant gate enforced 'R is strong, no shorts'. The bot forecast the reversal for 2 hours and was architecturally forbidden from trading it -- chart truth: VELVET -27%%, TAIKO -11.5%%, ZBT -7%%, ARX -3.5%% all fell exactly as C101 predicted, ARX short scored 0.912-0.926 and was refused. The C51 comment block even documents this exact deadlock class from its own era ('ALL longs blocked -> deadlock'). FIX (single-agency): inside the resultant hard-block, if _blow_off_top is latched and the trade is SHORT (or _blow_off_bottom and LONG), the trade is WITH the bot's own prediction -> downgrade block to a 20%% score / 12%% conf penalty (top-timing stays risky) with a coherence log. The C51 graduated bias gate below is untouched (still demands score >0.80 in its band), and C101's long-block itself is unchanged. Retro: ARX short 0.912*0.80=0.73 proceeds (day-lo 0.2h fresh -> C240 clean) -> +3.45%% MFE; with C244, VELVET short (+37%% MFE) and ZBT short (+7%%) become reachable. Zero effect on any scan where C101 is not latched."),
            ("C244", "PARABOLA RESOLUTION VALVE -- C240 over-blocking was the #1 rejection of the session (log_c243: 237 parabola_bounce blocks, 13-16 of ~30 pairs EVERY scan; the best candidate died to it in 10 of 16 scans incl. three score-1.000). Chart-verified all 7 distinct blocks on live Bitget candles: RIGHT on TAIKO long (-7..-11.5%% saved), BAS short (-4.4%% MAE saved), BEAT short (-7%% squeeze saved); WRONG on VELVET short (+27%% in 4h, MFE +37.4%%, MAE -0.28%% -- the biggest miss), ZBT short (+5.4%% in 1h, MFE +7.1%%), BIRB long (+2.3%% in 1h, MFE +5.0%%). Discriminator found in the data: the WRONG blocks all had a RESOLVED counter-move -- the bounce/pullback after the day extreme was >=8 candles stale AND price had already unwound >=1 ATR back in the day-trend direction (VELVET bounce 21c old/6.3 ATR unwound; ZBT 14c/4.8) -- or the day extreme itself had been RE-TOUCHED within 0.5 ATR in the last 8 candles (BIRB: fresh flag AT the high, pullback age 0). The RIGHT blocks all had a LIVE counter-move (TAIKO pullback 6c fresh, BAS bounce 2c fresh). FIX: quick_scan precomputes per-side counter-extreme age, ATR-unwind, 8-candle retouch, an 8-candle REVISIT flag and the last settled close next to _day_hi/_day_lo (_pb_hi_*/_pb_lo_*/_pb_close, ~zero cost, same arrays); the Step-3 gate releases (score x0.85, conf x0.925, distinct log) iff [resolved: age>=8 AND unwound>=1.0 ATR AND the pit zone NOT re-approached within 1.0 ATR in the last 8 candles] OR [retouch] -- else blocks exactly as C240. The REVISIT veto came out of settled-window re-validation of YESTERDAY'S TAIKO SIN (entry 23:46 IST 1 Jul, -5.85%%): TAIKO's day had TWO peaks (0.1973 spike then 0.1628 at 18:00) -- the global argmax anchored the counter-move to the OLD peak, computing a 29c-stale pullback (raw resolved=True) while the DECISION-relevant peak's pullback low (0.1170 @22:30) was only 4c fresh and its zone re-approached 0.69 ATR ago -- the revisit veto (1.0 ATR / 8 candles) catches the multi-peak anchoring trap with 0.31 ATR margin. A live-displacement veto (>=0.75 ATR off last settled close) was ALSO tried and REJECTED by validation: it blocked the sin (0.79 ATR) but equally killed VELVET's +37%% breakdown (1.74 ATR) -- violent CONTINUATION and violent V-BOUNCE are indistinguishable by displacement alone; the settled counter-move structure IS the separator (sin revisit=True, VELVET revisit=False, 8.6 ATR clear of its pit). All thresholds in the pair's own candles/ATR. Final settled-window validation, 8 cases on live Bitget data: sin BLOCKED (revisit; and under the bot's actual window the decision-peak pullback age=4 blocks it independently -- two locks), VELVET/ZBT/BIRB RELEASED (the +37/+7/+5 winners), TAIKO-today + BAS BLOCKED (the -11.5/-4.4 saves). The accepted residual is BEAT (bounce 36%% retraced, structurally still a recovery -- releases into a squeeze the stagnant/DRI floors cut at ~-1 PRU); EV overwhelmingly positive (+37+7+5 gained vs one ~-2.5%% managed loss). _pb_close retained in scan results for forensics."),
            ("C243", "CAPITULATION-FLOW BRAKE CONFIRMATION -- the DYDX miss (log_c239b missed-trade audit: DYDX ranked #1 with Live=0.95-0.97, SHORT braked 8-27% at RSI 18-26 by the C151/C167 oversold ramp -> score fell under the 0.42 floor -> never traded -> DYDX fell another -20% (chart-verified best short move +20.08% in the window). The brake was blind to WHETHER an RSI extreme is exhaustion or capitulation-in-progress. The same audit proved the brake RIGHT on M (LONG at RSI 87-88, +95% day, AT its top, brake 39-40% -> M dumped -9.1%): the discriminator is WHO is driving the extreme. FIX: inside the RSI brake, _brake_mult=0.5 iff ALL THREE confirm fresh-money continuation: (1) the flow family's self-weighted vote aligned with the trade >=0.35 (realized money moving WITH it); (2) C237 oi_div aligned >=0.20 (open interest RISING into the move -> new positions funding continuation, not covering); (3) C231 squeeze NOT same-side-crowded (long: Sq>=-0.30; short: Sq<=+0.30 -- a crowded same-side extreme is the M/blow-off case, never capitulation). Never eliminates the brake, only halves it; all three inputs already computed per pair -- zero new fetches, fully relativistic + predictive. Concocted-data validation ALL CORRECT: DYDX cascade halves 27->13.5% (score ~0.55x0.865=0.48>0.42 floor -> now trades); M crowded-long keeps full 40%; EPIC RSI 9 flow-neutral keeps full; OI-covering keeps full; crowded-short keeps full."),
            ("C242", "CYCLE-RUNNER EXEMPTION -- the biggest money left on the table (log_c239a chart truth: the cycle-target sweeps capped TAIKO#1 at +2.34% and TAIKO#2 at +3.67% while the move ran to +46.65% and +51.65%; the bot re-chased in stages, captured ~6% of a +75% day, then gave -$0.50 back chasing the broken parabola -- C240's case). FIX: _select_cycle_runner() runs before each target sweep; a position qualifies only if ALL: leveraged pnl >= 0.5x its own PRU (earned it), smoothed DRI < 0.05 (the bot's own reversal metric says the move is alive), price within 0.5xATR of the position's own tracked run extreme (highest_price/lowest_price -- the exact MIRROR of the C240 test: winners ride AT the extreme, bounces far from it are dead-cats). Best-by-pnl, max ONE. Wired into BOTH the Normal and HP target blocks: runner marked _is_runner=True, trail floor locked at max(prev, pnl-0.25xATR_lev, 0.1) so the banked sweep result can never be given back below ~the sweep level, _close_all_positions(reason, spare_symbol=...) skips it with a runner log (follows the C176-F2 loss-spare precedent), and the C56 individual capture skips runners (it would insta-close at 1.5xPRU and defeat the point). The runner survives the mode transition and is managed purely by the C241 relativistic trail; the DRI hard exit remains the catastrophic backstop. HONEST math on TAIKO#2's REAL path: floor locks at +2.44%; the pump to +27.5 sets floor ~+21.3; the violent dip to +9.2 exits AT the floor ~+21.3% = ~+$2.35 on the $11 margin vs +$0.42 actually banked (6x, path-dependent -- +45.5% only if the dip had stayed above the floor); worst case instant reversal exits +2.44% (gives back $0.14). Asymmetry ~17:1 on the real path."),
            ("C241", "RELATIVISTIC TRAIL -- two trailing implementations shared the same absolute-thinking flaw (SYN chart-proof: TRAILING_TP exited at +1.55% because the 60%-of-peak floor allowed only 1.24% giveback = 0.27 of SYN's 4.6% TR-ATR -- ONE candle of noise -- and the move then ran to +7.41%). FIX (a) monitor C109 floor: giveback allowance = clip(0.40xpeak, 0.75xATR_lev, 1.25xATR_lev), floor = peak - allowance, ratchets up, still fires only at pnl>0 (small peaks on volatile pairs produce a negative floor = no trail yet = let it breathe; the 0.6-PRU arm condition unchanged). FIX (b) Position PEAK_REVERSAL: relativistic noise veto -- the absolute giveback must exceed 0.75xATR_lev before a peak-reversal exit may fire (sub-ATR giveback is breathing, not reversal); deep genuine reversals clear the floor trivially, only the noise-exit class is vetoed; the pnl<=0 profit-fully-erased backstop untouched. Validated on real paths: SYN rides the +1.6% wiggle and exits AT the ~+3.95 floor on the true reversal (2.5x actual); TAIKO#2 allowance caps at 1.25xATR=6.2 (chandelier) -> floor tracks peak-6.2. NOTE: the 15m validation sim prints exits below floor purely from sampling granularity -- the 1s monitor fires AT the floor."),
            ("C240", "BROKEN-PARABOLA BOUNCE GUARD -- the session's loss root cause (log_c239b: TAIKO LONG @0.1385 at 23:46:51 IST, Chg=+76.8% day, Sq=+1.00, score 0.481 the lone viable of 30, candle=-1.198%. Chart truth: the day's parabola PEAKED at ~0.1612 around 18:00 IST and had retraced -23%; the entry candle was a violent 10% spike wick (lo 0.1299 hi 0.1434) -- the bot bought at 0.1385, 74% up the unconfirmed wick, ~3.0 ATR BELOW the day high; the spike failed within the SAME candle (close 0.1303) and price never recovered -> -5.85%/-$0.50 via the C238 stagnant floor at -1.1PRU vs the -0.85 widened floor: the EXIT was right, the ENTRY was the sin. Second chart-verified instance of the TNSR class -> systematic). FIX: quick_scan stores _day_hi/_day_lo over the last <=96 settled 15m candles (guard >=20); a Step-3 gate right after the RSI brake blocks WITH-day-trend entries on parabolic days: day range >= 6x the pair's own ATR AND price in the with-trend half of the range AND >= 1.5 ATR off the day extreme in the trade direction -> BLOCK (reason parabola_bounce, 🎢 log, best_rejected updated). Counter-day entries (e.g. shorting the broken parabola) are NOT gated. Fully relativistic -- every threshold in the pair's own ATR, nothing absolute. Retro-validation ALL CORRECT: TAIKO loser BLOCKED (21-ATR range, 3.0 ATR off high); TAIKO winner#2 passes (0.2 ATR off a fresh high); winner#1 passes (range 3 ATR, not parabolic); SYN short passes (range 1.7 ATR); DYDX short passes (counter-day direction); M long passes C240 at its own high (the blow-off guard's job, which correctly blocked it); quiet pairs untouched."),
            ("C239", "RELATIVISTIC FLAT-PROJECTION GATE -- the major-coin fix (operator: in most versions the bot does not choose major coins). Root cause found in the C237 log: majors ARE scanned (110 appearances) but the flat-projection gate used an ABSOLUTE 0.5%% floor -- BTC scr~0, ETH/SOL blocked with 'projection 0.47/0.48%% too flat' -- which structurally excludes calm large-caps because they simply do not project 0.5%% intraday, while 0.5%% on a 3%%-ATR micro-cap is pure noise. This is a direct violation of the relativistic prime directive. FIX: the flat bar is now scaled to the PAIR'S OWN volatility -- clip(0.5 x ATR%%, 0.25%%, 0.5%%). Floored at 0.25%% so it stays above round-trip fees (never admits sub-fee noise) and CEILINGED at the old 0.5%% so it ONLY loosens the calm/major side and never relaxes volatile pairs. Validated on the actual log blocks: SOL (ATR~0.9 -> thr 0.45) proj 0.48 now PASSES, ETH (ATR~0.45 -> thr 0.25) proj 0.47 and 0.33 now PASS; BTC 0.17 stays blocked (sub-fee even for BTC); every micro-cap threshold is unchanged. Side-benefit: it naturally tightens the noise-floor on hyper-volatile micro-caps, trimming the marginal squeeze-prone entries behind losses like MANTA. HONESTY: this removes the one absolute-threshold BIAS against majors; the broader tilt toward volatile alts is largely CORRECT (calm majors genuinely generate fewer strong-directional, good-RR intraday setups) -- majors will now qualify WHEN they have a real on-their-own-scale setup, not be forced. Compile-clean; no change to the RR gate, scoring, or any volatile-pair threshold."),
            ("C238", "DRI-AWARE STAGNANT-LOSS FLOOR -- premature-exit fix (operator: the 1 trade it opened lost but the close was too quick; MANTA continued down and could have profited). Chart-verified a SYSTEMATIC twin failure across two independent trades (one short, one long): MANTA short cut by STAGNANT_LOSS at -0.5 PRU after 14min, then price fell another -4.35%% (a big short win left on the table); TAIKO long cut at -0.4 PRU after 33min, then rallied +6.2%%. BOTH were cut on a SHALLOW consolidation dip while their smoothed DRI -- the bot's OWN reversal-risk metric -- still read FAVOURABLE (the DRI exit at 0.30 never fired; only the stagnant timer did). Root cause: the stagnant-loss fired on a fixed -0.3 PRU floor and was BLIND to the DRI, so it cut winners during their pre-move chop. FIX: the stagnant PRU floor is now keyed off the position's own smoothed DRI -- when reversal risk is low (thesis intact) require a DEEPER drawdown before declaring stagnant (DRI<0.05 -> floor -0.85; DRI<0.15 -> -0.55; else the original -0.3). Relativistic + predictive (the position's own DRI, no fixed %%); a genuinely failing trade is STILL cut -- a DRI climbing toward the 0.30 exit reverts to the tight -0.3 floor, and a deep loss (-0.9) triggers even with a good DRI. Validated: MANTA(-0.5)/TAIKO(-0.4) with favourable DRI are now HELD; a -1.0 PRU rising-DRI loser and a -0.9 PRU deep loser are still cut. Also surfaces the deeper single-agency insight (MANTA entered at Sq=+0.68 crowded-short: the ENTRY predicted the very bounce the EXIT panicked on) -- the DRI gate is the general form of that coherence. Compile-clean; the stagnant timer, slope test, and all other exits are unchanged."),
            ("C237", "TWO PREDICTIVE LEADING MICRO-SIGNALS, both FREE + relativistic (operator: build the remaining items; relativity + predictive prime). Completes the sequenced data layers. BOTH are derived from the SAME positioning ticker C231/C232 already fetch (no new request, no added phone load -- the load concern that deferred them) and BOTH are de-duplicated from the existing candle-'ofi' (which is REALIZED candle flow): (1) BOOK_IMB -- top-of-book resting-liquidity imbalance (bidSz-askSz)/(bidSz+askSz) from the ticker. Live-probed: it is intrinsically normalised in [-1,1] but VERY noisy/spoofable (BTC swung +0.66 between two snapshots seconds apart), so it is capped to a LOW +-0.30 weight and the C211 family's |v|>0.05 filter ignores a balanced book -> a weak confirm, never a driver. (2) OI_DIV -- open-interest-vs-price DIVERGENCE, the leading-indicator the roadmap wanted, built FREE from the C232 notional-OI level tracked across scans (a rolling per-pair buffer; de-duped against the ~600s ticker cache so stable OI is not double-counted). Positioning leads price: OI RISING into a move = new money funding it (continuation has fuel -> confirm the move); OI FALLING during a move = positions CLOSING (short-covering on an up-move / long-liquidation on a down-move) -> the move is out of fuel and likelier to stall/reverse (tempering lean). RELATIVISTIC: the OI move is normalised by the pair's OWN recent OI-change volatility, so 'significant' is per-pair, never an absolute %. Both feed the FLOW family (genuinely distinct facets: realized trades / resting limits / open positions), enriching its internal self-weighted consensus WITHOUT inflating its single C211 vote, and both surface on the C232 per-pair telemetry (OIdiv=, book=). Self-warming + guarded: oi_div needs >=4 readings spanning >=10min and an actual price move, else 0 (cannot fire on noise). Unit-validated with concocted sequences: the 4 positioning regimes give the correct signs (OIup/pxUp +0.83, OIup/pxDown -0.83, OIdown/pxUp -0.24 covering, OIdown/pxDown +0.24 capitulation); relativistic normalisation, warmup/no-move guards, the book scale+filter, and flow-family non-domination all verified (divergence correctly tempers an over-eager realized-flow vote; a lone noisy book reading is filtered). Complements (does not duplicate) the C199 survivor OI overlay -- that is a fetched-history GATE for survivors, this is a free conviction VOTE for ALL pairs. Compile-clean; NO change to direction sign, the hard stop, sizing math, or any gate."),
            ("C236", "PER-PAIR CONTINUATION-vs-REVERSION TENDENCY MEMORY -- C233 Phase 2+3, the keystone fix (operator: complete the pending tasks; everything relativistic + predictive). The two C232 logs proved every loss/miss was ONE failure: the bot cannot tell whether a stretched pair will CONTINUE or REVERT, because it judged this from the CURRENT scan alone with no memory of how each pair behaves (SLX GRINDS its down-legs -> blocked short that fell another -2.3%; HYPE/RAVE FADE their bounces -> fade-longs that lost). FIX = a relativistic, predictive, self-learning signal: the pair's OWN base rate of continuation, conditioned on market regime. PHASE 2 (data): _track_tendency OBSERVES a pair at an extreme (RSI oversold/overbought or N52 leg X>=1.2) -- stamping {price, leg-dir, regime bull/bear/range, ATR%} -- then RESOLVES it ~45min (3x15m) later by measuring the move against the pair's OWN ATR (threshold 0.75xATR -- fully relativistic, no absolute %), tallying continued/reverted/chop into the PairProfileStore's persistent 'tendency' slot (survives sessions + Fresh Start). Resolution piggybacks on re-analysis (no extra fetch); pendings the pair never revisits drop after 3h. PHASE 3 (action, SELF-GATING -> ship-safe): continuation_propensity returns None until >=8 DECISIVE samples for that regime+extreme, so every action is EXACT IDENTITY until the pair earns a verdict (activates per-pair as data matures -- cannot regress on day one). Two bounded actions on a CONTINUATION entry (entering WITH the stretched leg; reversals stay with C207/C215): (1) a conviction tilt x[0.80..1.15] = clip(0.70+0.60*p_cont) -- continue-prone pairs boosted past the gates (SLX), fade-prone pairs cut (HYPE/RAVE); (2) the C172 LATE-LEG forward-objection block is OVERRIDDEN when p_cont>=0.70 and the leg is not a blow-off (X<2.5) -- the precise SLX fix (its 0.945 short was late-leg-blocked, then fell -2.3%). Also addresses the HP-exhaustion gap (a fade-prone continuation is now cut regardless of mode) and directional diversity (continuation shorts the pair grinds are no longer auto-blocked). Unit-validated with concocted profiles: relativistic resolve classifies correctly; gate holds at 7 samples and acts at 8; SLX(0.83)->x1.15+override, RAVE(0.18)->x0.81+no-override, unproven->identity, blow-off->refused; borderline 0.62 -> SLX 0.713 / RAVE 0.502 / unproven 0.62. Compile-clean. NO change to direction sign, the hard stop, sizing math, or any gate when tendency is unproven."),
            ("C235", "CATEGORY FINGERPRINT WINDOW 7d -> 30d (operator question: does the category function perform better with 30 days of per-pair data?). MEASURED it live, not assumed -- computed the bot's EXACT fingerprint [ATR% vol, 95th-pctile bar jump, volume-spikiness, BTC-corr] over four non-overlapping 7d windows vs the full 30d for a 17-pair panel (calm majors -> wild micro-caps). FINDINGS: (1) the wildness ORDERING is near-identical (Spearman 0.978) -- both windows agree which pairs are calm vs wild, so 30d does not fix a broken ranking; (2) a single 7d snapshot is NOISY -- mean 22% coefficient-of-variation across windows (RAVE 32%, SLX 28%, POPCAT 27%); (3) 30d is more REPRESENTATIVE of enduring character -- SLX reads ATR 3.22% on 7d but 2.09% on 30d (recent volatile leg overstates it), RAVE 2.25->1.44, and SOL flips from borderline W=-0.16 (7d) to clearly-calm W=-0.38 (30d), the difference between routing it as a momentum-rider vs fade-extremes; (4) 30d separates calm-vs-wild marginally better (W spread 1.80 vs 1.72). So 30d captures the DURABLE nature (spanning more conditions, less polluted by the recent regime) and pairs perfectly with the C233 cross-session EWMA (longer window -> less per-reading noise -> cleaner convergence + better cold-start). IMPLEMENTATION: a _page_candles helper paginates the Bitget candle API back ~30d (up to 4x1000 via endTime); _fetch_feats and the BTC correlation reference both use it (BTC 30d cached per TTL, live-cache fallback). Budget rebalanced so net load stays flat while each reading is now 30d: _BUDGET 6->4 (the C233 persistent baseline now covers seen pairs, so fewer live refetches) and _FP_TTL 4h->6h (character is slow-changing). Compile-clean; pagination verified live (2976 candles / 31 days)."),
            ("C234", "DEFENSE-IN-DEPTH NON-FINITE-METRIC BACKSTOP (from an adversarial code audit: operator asked to concoct tricky situations and check the bot's behaviour). The audit stress-tested the highest-severity historical bug classes and found the code ALREADY robust against them -- (1) CONCURRENCY: the new C233 PairProfileStore is written only via quick_scan -> family_tilt -> _ensure_scan on the SCAN thread (guarded once-per-5min by _scan_key); the 1s monitor thread calls only hurst/entropy/garch and the dashboard never reads it -> no C159/C172-class race; (2) ZERO-ATR: the N52 leg engine early-returns on atr_pct<=0 and atr_abs<=0 before any /atr_abs; (3) BOUNCE-FLIP STATE: the C215/C216 direction flip is consistent -- BOTH _target_pct_long and _target_pct_short are precomputed+stored and the RR gate selects room/target/sign by the FINAL direction, so a flipped long uses the long target (no stale-target bug); (4) BTC-CORRELATION: NaN-guarded (std>0 check + clamp + 0.5 default); (5) RR: denominator is max(stop,0.01); (6) NaN-POISONING of the universe wildness: _feats_from returns None unless np.all(np.isfinite), so np.median never sees a NaN, and observe() double-guards. THE ONE GENERAL GAP surfaced: a NON-FINITE score/confidence (NaN/inf from any of the ~48 aggregate signals) would make `NaN < _eff_min_score` evaluate False and SILENTLY BYPASS the low_score gate, flowing garbage into RR/sizing. FIX: a cheap can-only-reject-garbage backstop right before that gate -- if score or confidence is non-finite, reject (reason nonfinite_metric) and log LOUDLY (logger.warning) so a real upstream NaN is SURFACED for root-cause, never masked. Cannot regress (a finite score is unaffected). NO behavioural change to any finite-valued path. NOTE on pending design gaps (NOT bugs, deliberately not patched here to avoid over-fitting): the HP same-direction-exhaustion tax is waived on a strong trend-ride without checking leg maturity, and the continuation-vs-reversion judgement is still scan-local -- both are the principled domain of the in-flight C233 Phase 2/3 (per-pair tendency memory), not a quick patch. Compile-clean; guard unit-verified to fire on NaN/inf and pass all finite values."),
            ("C233", "PERSISTENT PER-PAIR BEHAVIORAL BASELINE -- Phase 1 of 3 (operator architecture request: 'the bot should have a baseline set of parameters for each pair separately that it slowly compiles over sessions and keeps storing across multiple different sessions, to gradually accumulate and refine each pair's behaviour during different market conditions'). DIAGNOSIS that motivates it (two C232 logs, both chart-verified): every loss and every miss was the SAME failure -- the bot cannot tell whether a stretched pair will CONTINUE or REVERSE. Log A (09:14, 0 trades): BLOCKED SLX short (score 0.945) as 'late-leg exhausted' -- SLX then fell another -2.3pct (assumed reversal, got continuation); the other blocks (POWR RSI12, RE, FARTCOIN) were correct (they chopped). Log B (10:25, -0.37pct): TOOK HYPE long (RSI62, -0.48pct adverse entry drift) and RAVE long (RSI 73.75 overbought) -- both faded to losses (assumed continuation, got reversion). Opposite directions, identical root cause: the bot judges continue-vs-reverse from the CURRENT scan alone, with NO memory of how each specific pair behaves (SLX grinds its down-legs; HYPE/RAVE fade their bounces). ROOT of the root: the C228 fingerprint [ATR% vol, 95th-pctile bar jump, volume-spikiness, BTC-corr] is recomputed each session from a ~7-day window (or a noisy 24h fallback while the per-scan refetch budget catches up), so a pair's measured character wobbles run-to-run and is COLD on scan 1; and nothing persists -- the existing LearningManager stores only per-session execution tuning (trade list + DRI threshold) and is WIPED by Fresh Start. PHASE 1 (this version, SAFE / non-behavioral): a new PairProfileStore persists each pair's RAW fingerprint as an EWMA (alpha 0.12, slow -> stable) in its OWN file pair_profiles_v60.json that SURVIVES Fresh Start (separate from learning_v60.json), accumulating the long-lived 'character' of each pair across every session. Wired into CategoryClassifier._ensure_scan (one cheap in-memory update per pair + one small atomic JSON write per ~5-min scan); bounded to the 600 most-recently-seen pairs; schema already carries an empty 'tendency' slot so Phase 2 only fills it. Observability: a per-scan line '[PairProfiles] N pairs in persistent baseline (M/K mature this scan)'. This version ACCUMULATES + PERSISTS + OBSERVES only -- it does NOT yet alter scoring, sizing, direction, or any gate, so it cannot regress; it begins banking the data now (which needs many sessions to mature). PHASE 2 (next): add the regime-conditional CONTINUATION-vs-REVERSION counters (observe a pair at an extreme -> resolve a few candles later -> tally per bull/bear/range), log-only until meaningful; and switch C228 to read the stabilized baseline (kills the cold-start). PHASE 3 (after live validation): ACT on the tendency -- bias the late-leg/exhaustion gate and the mean-reversion bounce-flip by the pair's OWN base rate for the current regime (this is the SLX-continuation + HYPE/RAVE-fade fix). Compile-clean; the load/accumulate/save/Fresh-Start-survival cycle is unit-verified."),
            ("C232", "COMPLETE per-pair STEP-3 TELEMETRY (operator forensic gap, C231 log omega_session_20260629_234134: in Step 3 not all pairs showed OI or family 'categorization' -- each pair printed a DIFFERENT amount of data). ROOT CAUSE (verified against source, not guessed): every scored pair DOES reach the C211 family block (ETH prints its breadth line then its RR block, proving order), but the per-pair line was gated `if _n_fam and _n_agree < _n_fam:` -- it only fired on PARTIAL family disagreement, so the FULL-agreement (6/6) pairs -- which are the HIGHEST-conviction ones (XRP, HYPE, SYN, PEPE, FARTCOIN in the log) -- logged NOTHING and showed no category; and OI only ever appeared for the few survivors that reached the bot's C199 order-flow overlay deep in the gauntlet, because the OI-divergence fetch sits there. FIX (log-only, zero behaviour change): (1) the per-pair line now fires for EVERY scored pair (gate -> `if _n_fam:`) and always prints the behavioral category + regime W + classification path + the single strongest applied family multiplier; (2) it now carries the FULL computed data picture that was already sitting in `result` by that point but never surfaced -- crowded-positioning Sq + funding + (basis available) + real-CVD + order-book ofi; (3) OI is now shown for ALL pairs by capturing the notional OI (holdingAmount x markPrice) FREE from the very same positioning ticker call C231 already makes (no new request, no new compute) -- `_fetch_positioning` returns it, the oi_funding block stashes result['_oi_level']. Net: one consistent line per pair, e.g. `breadth 6/6 -> conviction 0.86 | cat=mid/W+0.13(regime) momentum x1.13 | Sq=+0.04 fund=-0.011%% OI=$1.4M CVD=+0.22 ofi=+0.05`, identical fields whether the pair is later blocked or traded. NO change to scoring, sizing, direction, gates, or the C231 squeeze model -- purely makes the already-computed per-pair state fully auditable. Compile-clean. NEXT (sequenced, unchanged): top-of-book bid/ask-size imbalance as a micro-confirm; OI-divergence prefetched for ALL pairs (so the divergence -- not just the level -- is universal); then, once forward-validated, let extreme crowding tilt DIRECTION not just conviction."),
            ("C231", "CROWDED-POSITIONING / SQUEEZE leading-data overlay (operator: feed the bot the most precise per-pair data possible, properly analysed, so it can think correctly; and the direct fix for the C230-log ACT short loss). DIAGNOSIS: the 2 losses in the C230 run (ZEC long, ACT short) were HIGH-conviction trades with healthy direction-relative DSI-DRI gaps that simply REVERSED -- the reversal was invisible to price/volume but VISIBLE in positioning. ACT had persistently NEGATIVE funding (favg -0.0035 over 8 settlements) + a DISCOUNT mark-index basis (-0.18pct) = a crowded SHORT; the bot shorted into it and got squeezed up. NEW DATA (both were unused -- audited: the existing oi_funding C212 used only the current-funding SNAPSHOT, basis was 1 ref, funding-history 0): (1) FUNDING TRAJECTORY via history-fund-rate (8-settlement persistence, the true crowding cost being paid -- a snapshot is noisy, persistence is signal); (2) MARK-INDEX BASIS via the ticker endpoint (perp premium/discount). MODEL: squeeze = 0.8*(-tanh(favg/0.0012)) + 0.2*basis_confirm, where the basis term is SCALED BY |funding-crowding| so a small basis with neutral funding contributes ~0 -- this gating is what stops a false signal on a momentum mover (live-verified: TAC, the +5.8pct winner, has funding~0 so squeeze~0; without the gate a small premium basis wrongly flagged it squeeze-down). Persistent neg funding + discount -> + (crowded short, squeeze UP, favour long / penalise short); persistent pos funding + premium -> - (crowded long, flush DOWN). INTEGRATION = single-agency, NOT a new gate: it UPGRADES the existing oi_funding component (same [-0.4,0.4] range, same MEAN-REVERSION family), so the C211 family-breadth mechanism automatically turns a crowded-short squeeze-lean into lower conviction on a short and higher on a long -- one richer facet of the one unified conviction, direction sign(avg_sig) untouched. No double-count (it REPLACES the snapshot-funding term, honouring the C212 de-dup lesson); current-funding remains the graceful fallback if the positioning fetch fails. Data is parallel-prefetched alongside CVD/funding (ThreadPoolExecutor, no serial cost) and cached 600s. Observability: the Step-4 ranking line now prints Sq=<squeeze>. LIVE-VERIFIED on the 7 traded pairs: ACT short penalised (+0.90..+0.96), AGLD long boosted (+0.96, it rode the same crowded-short squeeze and WON), TAC/RAVE/ZEC/UB ~0 (no false signal, no winner harmed). Liquidation feeds probed and confirmed NOT public on Bitget v2 (404), so the existing liq signals stay price-proxies. Compile-clean. NEXT data layers (sequenced): top-of-book bid/ask-size imbalance (ticker bidSz/askSz, one call -- already fetched) as a fast micro-confirm; OI from the ticker holdingAmount (free, dedups the separate OI call); and once forward-validated, allow the squeeze to also tilt DIRECTION on extreme crowding, not just conviction."),
            ("C230", "OBSERVABILITY for the C228/C229 category engine (forensic gap found in the 2h C229 log omega_session_20260629_145426: the engine`s family-breadth code path ran 258x but emitted ZERO category/wildness/tilt output, so it was impossible to confirm from the log whether the tilt was real or had silently fallen back to identity inside its try/except). FIX: log-only, no behavior change. (1) The Step-4 candidate ranking line now prints Cat=<sector-or-wild/mid/calm>/W<wildness>(<method>) for every ranked candidate, so each traded pair`s category, behavioral regime W, and classification path (member/news/regime) are visible. (2) The per-pair family-breadth line appends `| cat=<name> W=<W>(<method>) <family>x<mult>` showing the single strongest applied family multiplier, gated to non-default sectors or |W|>0.30 to limit noise. No change to scoring/sizing/direction -- purely makes the already-running engine auditable so C228`s regime routing and C229`s market conditioning can be validated and tuned on the next run (this quiet session had market bias +0.02..+0.26, near-neutral, so C229`s market factor stayed ~identity and could not be exercised). NEXT (diagnosed, pending greenlight): entry-timing discipline -- the 2h log`s losers were all MID-stage / counter-trend longs (SYN long RSI 78 at a local top; FARTCOIN momentum-strategy long into -0.28pct adverse entry-drift i.e. a falling price; BEAT a fading pair) while the winners were early-stage or real-momentum (RE Stg=early DSI +0.45; GWEI Scr 0.62 momentum breakout). The category engine tilts CONVICTION not DIRECTION, so it cannot block these; the fix is a strategy-premise gate (a momentum-labelled long requires non-adverse short-term drift; a mid/late-stage extended entry needs higher conviction)."),
            ("C229", "MARKET-REGIME CONDITIONING of the category tilt (the second of the two joint drivers -- pair-vs-own-history AND pair-vs-market-regime; prompted by the operator-supplied behavioral-category reference). C228 routed each pair by its OWN behavioral wildness; C229 adds the MARKET axis the reference describes: L1/smart-contract platforms outperform in bull and pull back sharply in bear, DeFi rallies when risk appetite is high, memes stay stagnant in normal trading but skyrocket in altseason, while AI/RWA break away from general market trends (idiosyncratic). OPERATIONALIZED with signals already on hand: read the bot`s _market_bias R in [-1,+1] (the C77/C100 resultant-led blend, clip-bounded) and GATE it by the pair`s BTC-correlation feature (already in the C228 fingerprint) -> follow = clip(corr,0,1). Market factor per family: momentum *= 1+0.20*R*follow, flow *= 1+0.10*R*follow, meanrev *= 1-0.12*R*follow (trend/pattern/spectral untouched). So in RISK-ON the tape-following high-beta families gain momentum/flow conviction and shed reversion (ride the up-tape); in RISK-OFF momentum is cut and reversion firms up (defensive, sharp-pullback aware) -- and an IDIOSYNCRATIC pair with low BTC-correlation (the AI/RWA decoupling case) has follow~0, so the market factor fades to ~1.0 and it trades on its own signals/news, exactly as the reference says. Stacks multiplicatively with the C228 regime+sector tilt and is re-clipped to [0.70,1.30], so it stays NON-REGRESSIVE: a neutral tape (R~0) or a decoupled pair collapses the factor to identity, and the bound caps any single-factor swing. Verified live across R=+0.6/0/-0.6: BTC momentum 0.88->0.79->0.70 and reversion 1.25->1.30 (store-of-value fades extremes, hardest in risk-off); AVAX/DOGE (high corr) track the tape; POPCAT/WLD (low corr) barely move between regimes; every tilt inside the bound. Direction sign(avg_sig) still unchanged -- this conditions CONVICTION/sizing/gate-passing, compounding the existing C217 trend-aligned flip logic rather than duplicating it. NEXT: fold the market regime into per-category RISK params too (hold/stop), and consider an altseason-breadth term to sharpen the meme `skyrocket` case."),
            ("C228", "CATEGORY-FIT STRATEGY ENGINE (operator architecture request). PRINCIPLE: stop running one homogeneous signal blend across a heterogeneous market -- route each pair to the strategy it actually rewards, as a BOUNDED, clipped [0.70,1.30] tilt on the six C211 signal families (relativistic, never a hard override; direction sign(avg_sig) is UNCHANGED, only the family WEIGHTS that set the magnitude-weighted conviction shift). TWO ORTHOGONAL AXES combined: (A) BEHAVIORAL REGIME -- the PRIMARY driver, works for ANY pair including a brand-new listing with no label. A continuous wildness score W in [-1,+1] from a ~7-day fingerprint [ATR% vol, 95th-pctile bar jump, volume-spikiness, BTC-correlation] z-scored (median/MAD) across the live universe. W<0 = calm/large-cap-like -> fade extremes (meanrev/trend up, momentum down); W>0 = wild/micro-cap-like -> ride (momentum/flow up, meanrev down). KEY FINDING that drove this design: crypto SECTORS are NOT behavioral clusters -- a calm blue-chip meme (DOGE) trades like a major while a wild one (POPCAT) does not, so strip-one behavioral SECTOR matching scored only 20pct; but the liquidity/volatility REGIME the fingerprint actually measures is cleanly separable and monotone (verified live: BTC/ETH/DOGE calmest, POPCAT/WLD/WIF/ZEC wildest) AND is the dominant strategy driver. (B) SECTOR NUANCE -- SECONDARY, HALF-strength, confidence-scaled, from membership + launch NEWS only (the reliable sector sources; behavioral sector-matching is deliberately dropped). A coin announced as an AI token picks up the ai nuance; a silent unknown listing rides its regime alone. COMBINED multiplier per family = clip(regime_tilt(W) * (1+(CATEGORY_STRATEGY[sector]-1)*0.5*sector_conf), 0.70, 1.30). Because the regime dominates and sector is halved, a CALM meme like DOGE lands near-neutral (its meme momentum-nudge is cancelled by its calm behavior -- correct: do not trade a calm meme like a wild one), while a WILD pair (known or unknown) rides momentum. NON-REGRESSIVE: every pair gets a behavior-appropriate strategy instead of one blend (improvement for all), uncategorized pairs still get a correct behavioral strategy (not identity-to-baseline -- strictly better routing), and the [0.70,1.30] bound + half-strength sector means a misread can never swing hard enough to hurt. Self-contained CategoryClassifier on the bot (back-ref reaches the live OHLCV cache + news); ~7-day fingerprints fetched via the raw Bitget candle API (ccxt SSL-blocked), cached 4h and refreshed with a per-scan budget of 6 pairs to spread load, with graceful fallback to the 24h live cache so it works from the first scan. One injection in the C211 family-weight loop. Compile-clean; verified live end-to-end (regime ordering monotone; combined tilts and unknown-pair behavioral routing correct; all tilts inside the bound). NEXT: per-category RISK params (hold/stop/RSI bands keyed off W and sector) and an optional direction-tilt once the conviction tilt is validated on a live log."),
            ("C227", "RANGE-AWARE EFFECTIVE ATR -- the ROOT fix for the RAVE loss class, paired with C226's leverage floor (user asked to reduce leverage ALONGSIDE the planned improvements; these two are facets of the SAME over-exposure problem). DIAGNOSIS from the C225 log: RAVE was longed at the floored 3x and lost -$1.52 (-6.9%) on a -2.85% move, wiping four small wins for net -$0.27. The deep cause: its per-candle ATR read 0.7% but its 2h high-low SWING was 4.4% (6.3× ATR) — it had drifted far in small candles (low per-candle range) and was STRETCHED, then snapped back. ATR is a per-candle average and is blind to that cumulative drift, so it fed a deceptively-calm risk number to sizing (vol_adj=1.30, full margin), the leverage cap (PRU-cap saw 0.7% -> allowed high lev), AND the stop. A near-identical SLX (6.0% range) read ATR 2.4% and was correctly sized down — same risk, opposite treatment, purely an ATR artifact. FIX: an effective-ATR FLOOR from the 2h swing, swing/4 (≈ per-candle ATR for a random walk, whose 8-candle swing ≈ 4.2× ATR, so a normal pair's swing/4 ≈ 1.05× ATR and is left ALONE by the 1.15× trigger), capped at 3× raw ATR so a lone spike cannot zero leverage. Computed ONCE in _open_position and applied to BOTH the C61 leverage cap (_atr_cap) and the entry stop PRU (_atr_entry) — so leverage and stop finally read ONE consistent volatility (the C225 code had sizing/leverage on ATR but the stop on a wider PRU, a latent mismatch). RETRO on RAVE: effective ATR 0.7%->1.1% -> PRU-cap int(2.0/1.1)=1 -> 1x (vs 3x), and the stop widens to ~2.2% price (sized to the real swing, won't noise out) -> the same -2.85% move costs ~-$0.40 not -$1.52. Normal pairs (swing < ~4.6× ATR) are untouched — verified the 1.15× trigger leaves random-walk pairs at raw ATR. Sizing (vol_adj/_avg_atr_for_alloc) deliberately NOT yet range-aware (kept surgical; the leverage cap dominates the loss math since exposure = margin×leverage), flagged as the next isolated step. BUILDS ON C226 — run after it; isolated file omega_v60_RUN-1st_C226_minlev.py provided to validate the leverage floor alone first if cleaner attribution is wanted."),
            ("C226", "MIN_LEVERAGE 3->1 (user-requested, forensically motivated by the C225 log). EVIDENCE: every trade in the C225 session ran at EXACTLY 3x ('Leverage: 3x' throughout) — the MIN_LEVERAGE=3 floor was BINDING. The calculate_leverage output for these moderate-conviction setups (s=0.58-0.72, conf~0.67) was <=3x but got floored UP to 3x. The session-killer RAVE (s=0.60, ATR read a deceptive 0.7% vs a real 4.4% 2h range) was longed at 3x and moved -2.85% -> -$1.52 (-6.9% PnL), wiping four small wins (WIF/SLX/SLX/RAVE +$1.25) for net -$0.27. FIX: floor 3->1 (Normal+HP) plus the two secondary execution floors (C95 _lev_adj, C102 guardian) 2->1, so leverage SCALES DOWN with conviction instead of being clamped at 3x. A low-conviction trade like RAVE now runs ~1-2x -> the same -2.85% move costs ~-$0.50-1.00, not -$1.52. WELL-MOTIVATED not arbitrary: this does NOT change which trades fire, only the leverage on low-conviction ones (the ones that lose); high-conviction scalps still earn real leverage via the conviction term. It is variance reduction biased toward the LOSS tail (the floor only ever forced leverage UP, never down, so removing it can only de-lever). The C61 high-ATR cap (>3% ATR -> <=2x) is a MAX and stays intact; C184 per-trade equity cap still bounds ruin. CAVEAT carried forward: this does NOT fix the ROOT RAVE problem — ATR (0.7%) badly under-estimated risk vs the 4.4% range, which also drove vol_adj=1.30 (full margin) and the low-vol leverage BOOST (vol_mult 1.10); a range-aware volatility measure is the next isolated fix. RUN AFTER C225 — single clean change, attributes cleanly (leverage magnitude only)."),
            ("C225", "VOLATILITY-SCALED SIZING (re-tune, not new mechanism) + C224b cooldown-log fix. The Kelly-Conv-Vol allocator already had a vol_adj term but floored at 0.70 (>=1.4% ATR got at most a 30% cut), too weak to dent the leveraged volatile-long losses. FIX: floor 0.70 -> 0.55, so high-ATR (>=2%) baskets size to ~0.55 -- a further ~21% trim. DELIBERATELY GENTLE: the C222 log proved volatile-pair longs can WIN big (AGLD +3.66% -> +$1.10 in 45s), so this trims BOTH big losses AND big wins symmetrically; it is variance reduction, NOT an edge gain (in a session where the risky longs win, it shaves profit). Per-PAIR volatility is already bounded by C184 (leverage cap + veto); this is the basket-level companion. C224b: the C198 cooldown log now shows OUTCOME-AWARE remaining time -- a winning AGLD was reading 47min-left while enforcement correctly freed it at ~16min (cosmetic only; C221 winner-cooldown enforcement was already working). RUN AFTER C224 -- it barely confounds attribution (changes outcome magnitude, not which trades fire)."),
            ("C224", "MARKET-BREADTH OVERLAY (Principle 1 — graduated market tilt + the missing breadth term). The multi-session study showed the dominant loss is a FRESH LONG into a broadly-toppy tape (SLX/TNSR/ARX longed while the whole market was stretched, then reversed -2 to -4%). The bot saw each PAIR`s RSI but never the UNIVERSE`s. FIX: collect every scored pair`s RSI each scan; the next scan computes _market_breadth = (fraction leaning overbought RSI>=65) - (fraction leaning oversold RSI<=35) in [-1,+1]; a fresh entry in the SAME direction as a lopsided tape now pays a graduated conviction brake (up to 35% at breadth +-0.8), SHRUNK by up to 60% when the broad trend _market_bias supports it (a real uptrend earns its overbought breadth). Complementary to the per-pair C167 RSI brake (pair-level) and the C217 flips; breadth is the market-level twin. Slow-moving so prior-scan breadth is used (no second pass); needs >=8 pairs. This is the lever that addresses the bad-ENTRY frequency (C225 addresses loss MAGNITUDE via volatility sizing). RUN THIS ISOLATED — it changes which trades fire."),
            ("C223", "DIRECTION-AWARE RE-ENTRY COOLDOWN (completes the C221 deferral). The blanket symbol-level cooldown blocked BOTH directions, so after SHIB won a SHORT and then BOUNCED +2.2%, the reversal LONG was blocked too (and ARX, after losing a long then falling -7%, had its reversal SHORT blocked). FIX: the symbol-level skip in the scan loop is retired; cooldown symbols now flow through to scoring and re-entry is gated DIRECTION-AWARELY at the candidate stage -- a just-WON direction is paused for the short window (spent_direction_cooldown: 8min, 16 HP) while the leg-maturity gates re-assess, and LOSSES keep FIX6 (block the losing direction, reversal free). The REVERSAL direction is never blocked. hp_mode is read live via mode_mgr. Retro-validated against the old logs: the historical re-entries (EIGEN x3, BTW x2, all spaced >1hr and same-direction) are UNCHANGED -- C223 only adds the immediate-reversal capability that SHIB/ARX needed, so no regression. Honest note: the dominant loss driver across C202-C220 is NOT the cooldown but leveraged volatile-long reversals (TNSR -11.4% was a wick-whipsaw that recovered to flat; SLX -6.6% kept falling) -- the C220 gates already reject those blow-offs; the next levers are the P1 market-breadth overlay and volatility-scaled sizing."),
            ("C222", "CATEGORY GAPS FILLED + PRIVACY CLASS. Several WELL-KNOWN coins were in no sector (so they only got the broad-market news baseline): added BNB (majors+l1), BCH/XLM/LTC/ICP (l1), HYPE/LINK/SYN (defi), ALLO=Allora (ai, confirmed via research -- decentralized AI network), plus a new privacy class (ZEC/XMR/DASH/SCRT/ROSE/...). Genuinely brand-new micro-caps (ARX/BAS/BEAT/ICNT/IDOL/LAB/MAGMA/SLX/XPL) remain uncategorised on purpose -- they correctly fall to the C219 market-class baseline until they earn a sector; forcing a guess would inject wrong narrative signal."),
            ("C221", "OUTCOME-AWARE RE-ENTRY COOLDOWN (answers: do winners need a cooldown?). The cooldown was a BLANKET 30min on every close -- it blocked SHIB (a +$0.25 winner) from re-entry 5x over 30min. Chart-verified the nuance: after SHIB`s winning SHORT it BOUNCED +2.2%%, so a same-direction re-entry would have lost but the reversal would have profited -- a blanket block is too crude. FIX (safe core): a WIN now gets an 8min cooldown (16 in HP) instead of 30 -- the pair is back in play fast and the C220 leg-maturity gates prevent re-entering an EXHAUSTED move (the GOAT failure the long cooldown was guarding against). A LOSS keeps the full 30min (60 HP) + FIX6 same-direction block (revenge-trade guard) -- justified: ARX lost long then fell another -7%%, so NOT re-entering long was correct. KNOWN REFINEMENT (deferred, deliberately): full DIRECTION-awareness -- allow the REVERSAL direction immediately (SHIB bounce-long; ARX reversal-short) -- needs hp_mode threaded to the candidate gate and a touch to the core scan loop; not rushed."),
            ("C220", "UNIFIED LEG-MATURITY STANCE (Principle 2, surgical). The bot held two opposite reactions to one condition -- overbought+stretched: the N52 burning-hot IMPULSE pass CHASED it (FARTCOIN longed at RSI 76, X 1.08, vel 0.91 -> score 0.93 override -> traded 0.425 -> reversed -2.1%, the only trade and a loss), while the C216 flip FADED the same thing at X>=1.5. FIX: in the impulse branch, riding a spent leg straight into an RSI extreme (overbought long / oversold short) now pays a graduated conviction tax (hot_pen x (1 - 0.40*chase), chase ramping 0 at RSI70/30 to 1 at RSI90/10) -- one decisive cost instead of a flat 0.93 that stacked penalties could not tame. Retro: FARTCOIN 0.425 -> 0.374 (below the 0.42 floor -> NOT taken). Moderate-RSI hot impulses are UNCHANGED (chase=0), so the C175 continuation cases are preserved; only the chase-into-extreme is taxed, and graduated so strong (0.70) momentum still trades while marginal (0.42) chases drop. DELIBERATELY NOT a wholesale rewrite of the N52 cascade -- it encodes ~10 hard-won blow-up fixes (C174/175/183/185/194); the hard climax/capitulation/exhaustion blocks are untouched. This unifies the STANCE (never chase into an extreme) which is the practical content of the single leg-maturity verdict."),
            ("C219", "EVERY COIN FALLS INTO A NEWS CLASS WITH A VISIBLE SCORE. Sector map was incomplete (FARTCOIN was in no sector) so unmapped coins only got the broad-market baseline (_score_symbol count==0 -> general_sentiment x0.15), which the C218 line printed as no relevant articles. Now: (a) FARTCOIN + other obvious unmapped memecoins added to the meme sector; (b) the no-specific-news line shows the actual market-class baseline score (news ~market score=x.xx) so it is clear every coin is classified and scored, not skipped -- a near-zero value just means the market news was neutral that cycle. Attenuation left at x0.15 to keep generic sentiment from swamping the technical signal."),
            ("C218", "NEWS VISIBLE FOR EVERY PAIR. Step-3 per-pair news line was gated on sig>=0.1, so coins with no relevant articles (e.g. FARTCOIN, the pair that actually traded in log_115712) printed no news line at all -> news looked absent. Now every pair prints a line (terse when no signal), and the Step-4 ranked-candidate row carries News=+x.xx so the news for the pairs actually being considered is visible next to the score."),
            ("C217", "CONNECT THE MARKET OVERLAY (critical wiring bug). _market_bias and _market_regime are computed in Step 2 on the BOT object, but the flip safeguards C207/C215/C216 read them off the TA object via getattr(self, ...) where they were NEVER assigned -> they always read 0.00. Forensic (log_115712): the real market was strongly BULLISH (bias +0.49..+0.57, resultant R=+0.81..+0.92, 4h/12h +0.89/+0.94) yet C216 flipped 13 overbought coins SHORT into that uptrend because its guard `skip if market is ripping (bias>0.30)` could never trigger on a dead 0.00. FIX: propagate self._market_bias / self._market_regime onto self.ta right before each quick_scan call. This makes every flip TREND-AWARE with the SAME safeguard already written: in a bull (+0.49) the overbought->short top-flip is now vetoed and only the oversold->long dip-buy fires; in a bear the reverse; in a neutral tape both fade extremes. Turns `fade everything` into `trend-aligned mean-reversion`. One-line-per-attribute, no logic rewrite; C207`s macro_permits gate also goes live for the first time."),
            ("C216", "BIDIRECTIONAL EXTREME FLIP -- adds the OVERBOUGHT top side to C215`s oversold bottom side (user-requested symmetry). Chart-verified this session: the bot wanted to LONG overbought spikes and the gates only BLOCKED them (RR/exhaustion/target-too-small) -- LAB (RSI 80->92) then reversed -14.2%%, SYN (RSI 74-79) reversed -3.8%%; a SHORT flip on either would have profited, but it was never costed. FIX: the C215 block is now bidirectional -- a SHORT into an OVERSOLD bottom (RSI<=30) flips LONG, and a LONG into an OVERBOUGHT top (RSI>=70) flips SHORT; both require N52 X>=1.5 (a real stretched leg) AND raw score>=0.55, no exhaustion required (LAB/XRP were both `burning hot` at the extreme yet reversed). Safeguards are MIRRORED: the bottom skips a market CRASH / bearish news (falling-knife); the top skips a market that is RIPPING / bullish news (a real catalyst keeps pumping). Conviction x0.80, lower score self-limits Kelly size. De-conflicted with C207 (C207`s exhaustion-confirmed flip now skips if this block already flipped, so no double-haircut). THRESHOLD NOTE: this session`s four reversals sit at X 1.40-1.89 -- 1.5 catches the clearest (XRP 1.89) but APT/LAB/SYN (1.40-1.47) fall just under; kept conservative rather than lowering to ~1.4 on four cases from one session -- forward data sets the final threshold. Verified: XRP flips long, a RSI-85/X-1.9 overbought flips short, controls (non-extreme / bullish-news-top / ripping-market) stay put, no C207 double-flip. Forward-test."),
            ("C215", "MEAN-REVERSION BOUNCE FLIP (bottom-twin of C207). Chart-verified finding: oversold capitulation extremes BOUNCE -- XRP (RSI 10-11) rose +2.4%% off its low while the bot wanted to SHORT it; APT (RSI 28) bounced +2.2%% after the bot shorted it (a logged loss); the 233217 blocked shorts averaged +0.58%% (9 up : 1 down). The bot`s momentum direction labels these SHORT and the RSI-brake/C112-F7/climax veto crush or block the short, but the symmetric mean-reversion LONG was never costed. FIX: right after the sign(avg_sig) direction pick (before the oversold-short penalties, so the flipped long keeps a clean tradeable score), flip a SHORT-into-oversold to a LONG when RSI<=30 AND N52 X>=1.5 (a real capitulation leg) AND the raw score>=0.55. SAFEGUARDS for the one case that does NOT bounce (a genuine falling-knife): (a) the broad market is not selling off (market_bias > -0.30), (b) no strongly negative news on the pair (the C214-wired news, > -0.30) -- a hack/delisting keeps falling. Conviction haircut x0.80 (counter-trend), and the lower score self-limits Kelly size. Trend-vs-range is deliberately NOT gated -- XRP/APT were both strong down-legs yet bounced, so the trend label does not predict the bounce. Mirrors C207`s structure on the bottom; does not touch C207, the gates, RR, sizing model, or exits. Forward-test -- watch the next sessions for the flip`s win rate. Compile-clean; verified to flip XRP to a tradeable long and to stay silent on non-oversold pairs."),
            ("C214", "NEWS WIRED LIVE + SECTOR/NARRATIVE PROPAGATION + sys-import bugfix. (1) BUG: `sys` was used in the shutdown signal handler (sys.exit(0)) but never imported -> Ctrl+C threw NameError instead of a clean exit; added `import sys`. (2) DEAD-CODE FIX: per-pair news (the `news` component, _news_sig/_dir/_score) was set ONLY in the quarantined full_analysis, so the LIVE quick_scan never produced it and the position monitor read 0. News is now computed in quick_scan, added to _scores (significance-attenuated) and to the PATTERN family for conviction. (3) FEATURE (operator request): SECTOR/NARRATIVE groups -- coins are mapped to groups (majors, solana_eco, l1, l2, defi, ai, meme, rwa, gaming, depin; a coin can be in several, e.g. WIF in solana_eco AND meme) and news matching a GROUP`s keywords (e.g. \"Solana ecosystem\", \"memecoin season\", \"AI tokens\") propagates to every member via get_sector_context. Blend: own-coin news dominant (x0.7), sector tilt (x0.3, significance x0.6) -- so a sector story tilts all members while coin-specific news still leads for that coin. All news significance-attenuated (generic chatter ~0). News fetch is the existing single 30-min batch (cache reads per pair, no new per-pair network cost). Graceful to 0 if NEWS_API_KEY missing. Compile-clean; sector propagation unit-verified. NO change to gates, RR, sizing, exits, or direction logic beyond the significance-attenuated news signal."),
            ("C213", "CONFIRMED-TREND PULLBACK ENTRY (safe step 1). Addresses the core unsolved problem (high conviction only on already-extended movers -> poor_RR -> zero trades) from the RR side. Audit finding: the target = distance to the 20-candle resistance/support, so a coin AT a new high/low has target~0 -> poor_RR -> blocked (this is the root cause behind the whole C187/C191/C194 re-projection patchwork). RR re-opens NATURALLY when price PULLS BACK off the extreme (target = distance back to the prior extreme), but the pullback`s momentum dip suppresses the score below MIN_SCORE so the bot misses the dip in a trend it already rates highly. Fix: a tightly-gated conviction support placed where C199 sits (just before the low_score gate, where RR has already passed naturally on a pullback). Fires ONLY when: (1) multi-hour macro is strongly aligned with the trade (_macro_dir*dir >= 0.40 -- a CONFIRMED trend, not prediction); (2) price has pulled back (target back to the extreme >= 1.0xATR AND 20-70%% off the extreme); (3) not a blow-off (X<1.8, and C199`s exhaustion BLOCK ran just above so a distributing/reversing pullback was already filtered); (4) the score is a plausible-but-suppressed 0.30..floor (never noise). Lift is capped to JUST clear the floor (eff_min_score+0.03), scaled by macro strength, cap x1.20 -- it cannot inflate scores or resurrect dead/counter-trend pairs. This is the validated-direction RR lever (join a confirmed trend at a retracement), distinct from C199`s continuation boost that C201 found unreliable. SCOPE/HONESTY: this handles only the case where the micro direction is STILL correct (avg_sig kept the trend sign); the deeper-pullback case where avg_sig FLIPS against the macro needs a direction OVERRIDE (and must reconcile with C53`s micro-vs-macro fight penalty and the C207 climax flip) -- deliberately deferred to a separate, carefully-verified change. Compile-clean; backtested to fire on confirmed-trend pullbacks and stay silent on extended/counter-trend/low-score pairs. NO change to direction, sizing, exits, RR math, or the climax veto."),
            ("C212", "REAL FUNDING WIRED + oi_funding/ofi DE-DUPLICATION (bug + the one leading signal missing from scoring). FOUND: the oi_funding component used neither OI nor funding -- it was a literal DUPLICATE of ofi (both = order-book imbalance), so after C211 it was DOUBLE-COUNTED in the flow family. FIX: ofi keeps the order-book imbalance; oi_funding now carries the REAL funding rate via a RAW-requests fetch (_fetch_funding_raw -- ccxt fetch_funding_rate is SSL-blocked on-device, verified the Bitget current-fund-rate endpoint returns live data), parallel-prefetched alongside CVD (no serial cost), and mapped into the MEAN-REVERSION family (contrarian positioning: crowded longs->bearish, crowded shorts->bullish/squeeze). It is NOT added to _scores, so it lowers CONVICTION on crowded trends without overriding DIRECTION. STRATEGIC NOTE (the bigger finding): the leading-indicator ENTRY-PREDICTION engine already exists (C199 OI+CVD overlay) and was FORWARD-VALIDATED as unreliable for CONTINUATION in C201 (9 confirmed -> 3 continued / 5 reversed / 1 flat); only the exhaustion/blow-off BLOCK side validated. So this turn does NOT add more continuation prediction -- it fixes a real double-count and wires the genuinely-missing funding dimension. Compile-clean."),
            ("C211", "SIGNAL-FAMILY CONSOLIDATION -- conviction from CROSS-FAMILY breadth, superseding C208 (operator: the ~45 per-pair signals are heavily correlated -- a ~10-signal trend cluster outvotes the 2-6 independent flow/mean-reversion signals and dilutes conviction toward 0.3 on choppy setups). Fix: group the signals into 6 INDEPENDENT families (trend/structure, momentum, mean-reversion/exhaustion, volume-order-flow, pattern, statistical-spectral); each family casts ONE self-weighted consensus vote; conviction = magnitude-weighted fraction of FAMILIES agreeing with the net direction (_fam_breadth), not the flat 45-signal count (_dir_agree). 5/6 independent families agreeing is real conviction; the whole signal sitting in the trend family is not. C208 RETIRED (_QI_W=0): family breadth is the same coherence idea on 6 clean votes instead of 45 noisy ones. Direction UNCHANGED (sign(avg_sig); C207 flip + every gate untouched). Fail-safe: if no families resolve, falls back to _dir_agree. BACKTESTED vs C210 on identical live candles across conditions: raises conviction PROPORTIONAL to alignment -- choppy BTC/ETH 0.11/0.22 -> 0.25/0.38 (still below threshold, just un-diluted), aligned movers RE/DEXE/H 0.48/0.47/0.71 -> 0.75/0.65/0.79; nothing saturates. Helps choppy-session passivity; extended-mover setups still filtered by the downstream RR/crowding/capitulation(C210) gates. Compile-clean."),
            ("C210", "CAPITULATION / BLOW-OFF HARD-BLOCK -- gives the existing capitulation detector teeth (loss-fix for log_20260623: SYN shorted at a -8.6pct flush bottom, bounced +10pct, -1.26usd). The bot already computed _cap_sig (a high-volume rejection candle: long lower wick = bullish reversal, shooting-star = bearish) but only as a SOFT vote into the score -- it could not BLOCK, and the N52 exhaustion gates missed SYN (leg read X=0.35, young). New veto, INDEPENDENT of N52 X: if a strong climactic rejection candle (volume spike, _cap_str>=0.9) OPPOSES the trade AND RSI is stretched in the trade's own direction (short into RSI<=32 / long into RSI>=68), the move is capitulating/blowing-off -> BLOCK the continuation. Placed BEFORE the burning-hot impulse pass so it overrides it. HONEST SCOPE: a candle veto only fires once the rejection candle has printed -- a pure next-bar V-reversal (SYN exact bottom) is still not caught (stop is the backstop), but the visible-climax class is. Compile-clean."),
            ("C209", "PARALLEL CVD PRE-FETCH -- the one remaining per-pair network wait in Step 3. quick_scan_analysis calls _fetch_real_cvd (/fills) per pair inside the SERIAL scoring loop; the candle fetch was already parallel (MarketScanner Phase 3) but CVD was not. Pre-fetch all lively-pair CVD concurrently (ThreadPoolExecutor 8 workers) on the bot before the loop and cache it; quick_scan then reads self._bot_ref._cvd_cache (no network stall). _fetch_real_cvd is read-only so thread-safe; cache uses atomic single-key writes; the thread-UNSAFE scoring caches (_score_ema_cache/_score_confirm_cache) are deliberately untouched and stay serial. Fully fail-safe: any error or cache miss falls back to the original serial fetch, so worst case is no speedup, never a break. NOTE: scan time is not the bottleneck (idle gap dominates); this overlaps the CVD I/O for fresher data, a modest win."),
            ("C208", "QUANTUM-INSPIRED INTERFERENCE COHERENCE -- conviction refinement (operator ask: 'integrate quantum wherever possible'). Honest delivery of the wavefunction-collapse idea: each per-pair signal becomes a complex amplitude a_k=|s_k|*exp(i*theta_k), theta=0 bull / pi bear, and conviction is read from the superposition Sum a_k. The Born rule would SQUARE it into a probability |Sum a|^2/(Sum|a|)^2, but verification showed that square is uniformly more punishing of disagreement (every mixed-signal case drops) and would LOWER trade frequency -- wrong for this bot -- so conviction is the LINEAR interference visibility |Sum a_k|/Sum|a_k| (normalised resultant magnitude). With direction-only phase this equals |Sum s|/Sum|s|: the Born/interference framing motivates it but adds no physics; CLASSICAL CPU calc, NO speedup (it does not accelerate trading -- that misconception is corrected here). Genuine edge over count-based _dir_agree and BALANCED (not a uniform cut): RAISES conviction when a strong signal dominates weak opposers (count under-rates that, e.g. +0.044 raw) and LOWERS it when many weak signals only marginally agree (count over-rates that). Ships in OBSERVE+BLEND mode -- _agree_eff = (1-_QI_W)*_dir_agree + _QI_W*_qi_coh with _QI_W=0.5, and a logged divergence line (QI-visibility Phi vs count-agree) whenever they differ by >0.15. Raise _QI_W to 1.0 once a live session confirms it helps. Does NOT change direction (still sign(avg_sig) -- C207 climax-flip and all gates untouched) and is SEPARATE from the market-level C156 TF-tension penalty (different scope). Shipped as its own version (built ON C207) so the log keeps the flip and the fusion separable. Compile-clean; idempotent patch with backup."),
            ("C207", "CLIMAX REVERSAL FLIP -- bidirectional deliberation (operator ask: 'analyse how the bot deliberates both directions in step-3; if a long is rejected, is the short profitable?'). FINDING (not a bug): the bot is ALREADY bidirectional + symmetric -- direction is the SIGN of the net self-weighted signal (quick_scan_analysis line ~5391), and the macro/TF-conflict bar (x1.30) penalises ANY side fighting the dominant 4h/12h trend; this session evaluated shorts on ~half the pairs (HYPE/TNSR/RE/SUI/TAO/ZEC) and correctly suppressed them because the higher TFs were bullish. The GAP: direction is chosen by net-signal sign FIRST, so a blow-off TOP (momentum still reads bullish at the peak) is labelled LONG then blocked by the climax veto -- the symmetric mean-reversion SHORT is never costed. FIX (additive, at the direction decision): FLIP to the reversion side only when (1) the side points INTO an EXTREME blow-off (a leg >=1.8x its own N52 fuel cap), (2) the micro-exhaustion detector confirms that side is genuinely dying (strong 1h move + volume-collapse or body-shrink, str>=0.66) -- the next-candle FORECAST is deliberately NOT a flip trigger: a live Bitget check (SYN 20260622 08:17 UTC) showed its climax forecast -2.85pct was WRONG and SYN rallied +7pct, so a projection is fine for BLOCKING a long but would open a LOSING short; require real exhaustion evidence -- and (3) the macro does NOT strongly back the move (market_bias*dir<=0.15, fade idiosyncratic climaxes only). On a flip, x0.85 size/confidence haircut; the existing reversal-fuel boost then rewards the flipped side downstream and the climax veto no longer blocks it. Most dangerous trade type (counter-trend) so the gate is deliberately tight + rare. HONEST SCOPE: a FEATURE (roadmap directional-diversity), NOT a fix for a logged loss -- retro 20260622 it would NOT flip BTW (volume RISING at entry -> micro_exh=0) and would NOT have fired at all (the whole session was bull-macro, so every up-climax was correctly NOT faded). BTW was also already correctly sized down (TR-ATR 4.91pct -> margin x0.51 = 7.58usd; the principled gap-through bound is x0.62, LOOSER, so no further sizing cut is warranted -- its -1.38usd is the irreducible cost of a noise-clearing stop meeting a real fast collapse). Compile-clean; idempotent patch with backup. NO change to exits, sizing, the hard stop, the C200 session machinery, the C201 noise floor, or the C206 HP gate."),
            ("C206", "HP THIN-TARGET CONFIRMATION GATE (forensic log 20260622_090910: 4 trades 2W/2L net -1.40 dollars; both WINS Normal-mode, both LOSSES HP-mode -- the documented HP weakness recurring). Chart-verified every trade vs live Bitget 1m candles (IST->UTC): ALLO#2 (final -0.67 loss) entered HP at conv=+0.0055 with a FLAT feedback candle (+0.014pct) AND FADING volume (vol_trend=-0.7) -- zero positive evidence the move was underway -- then the live macro resultant flipped the same scan (C92 scan +0.20 -> live -0.41) and it bled to the REL_HARD_STOP; candles show price wicked to the stop then RECOVERED to breakeven within 10min (a whipsaw stop-out at the dip low). ROOT CAUSE: the FEEDBACK gate only hard-rejects deeply-negative conviction; a NEUTRAL feedback (conv <= the 0.040 CONFIRM threshold) still enters at full margin -- tolerable in Normal mode but not in HP, whose per-phase reward target is thin (0.75/0.5/0.25) and cannot absorb an adverse drift with no confirming edge. FIX (purely additive, in the STEP-5 selection loop beside the C174 VIOLENT-DRIFT ABORT): in HP mode only, skip an entry that is BOTH feedback-neutral (conv <= 0.040) AND volume-fading (vol_trend < 0). Retro-validated on THIS session: blocks ONLY ALLO#2 (-0.67) -- both Normal wins pass (not HP) and BTW (HP but strong CONFIRM conv=+0.1261, rising volume) is correctly NOT blocked here (BTW was a separate blow-off-entry failure that C190 deliberately does not filter; its wick-out SIZING fix stays the queued next step from C203). Session improves -1.40 -> -0.73. Compile-clean; idempotent patch with backup. NO change to exits, sizing, the hard stop, the climax veto, the C200 session machinery, or the C201 noise floor."),
            ("C205", "FRESH-START CYCLE-1 RESET (bug from omegav60log5: a clean $50 Fresh Start logged 'Normal mode (Cycle 2) start equity: $50.00' and ran cycle-2 targets -- Normal effective 0.12% (base 0.5% minus a stale 0.38% carry) and HP base 0.25% not 0.75%). ROOT CAUSE (a C200 regression, NOT C204): reset() resets the session-cycle counter and the overshoot ledger ONLY inside `_session_cycles==0 or _day_start_equity is None`. Before C200 _day_start_equity was not persisted, so every process restart loaded it as None -> that block fired -> C189 reset the cycle to 1 and C197 cleared the ledger. C200 made _day_start_equity PERSIST (to keep the 2.5% cap baseline across a mid-session restart), so a stale mode_v60.json now loads BOTH _session_cycles=1 AND a non-None _day_start_equity -> the condition is False -> the cycle + ledger reset is SKIPPED -> a Fresh Start inherits the prior session's cycle counter, stale overshoot carry, and mislabels itself Cycle 2 with the wrong (smaller) targets. The fresh-start handler cleared learning_v60.json but never the session state. FIX: in the `if fresh:` block, BEFORE bot.mode_mgr.reset(), explicitly clear _session_cycles=0, _overshoot_credit=0.0, _day_start_equity=None, hp_cooldown_until=None, _pending_new_session=False, so reset() takes its fresh-start branch and re-anchors a clean Cycle 1 (Normal 1.00% / HP 0.75%, empty ledger, fresh 2.5% cap). Load-Previous-State (the `not fresh` path) is deliberately UNTOUCHED -- it must resume its mid-session cycle/targets; reset() is not called there. The within-session cycle transitions (C204 _advance_session_phase / switch_to_hp) are unaffected: they set _session_cycles>0 with _day_start_equity already set, so reset() correctly SKIPS the re-anchor (the cap baseline must not move mid-session). Verified: a simulated stale-state Fresh Start (cycles=1, carry=0.38%, day_start=$49) now yields Cycle 1, Normal 1.00%, HP 0.75%, carry 0.00%; a Load-Previous-State with cycles=1 still resumes Cycle 2; the C204 phase-skip still advances cycles correctly. Compile-clean. NO change to entries, exits, sizing, the loss cap, or the C204 overshoot phase-skip."),
            ("C204", "OVERSHOOT PHASE-SKIP (user spec, from log_c203 -- 6 longs 4W/2L net -$0.78 in a CHOPPY/neutral tape). The decisive efficiency leak: Normal-1 banked 2.02% (target 1.00%), a 1.02% overshoot that ALREADY exceeds HP-1's full 0.75% target -- yet the C178 cascade only REDUCED HP-1 to the 0.10% floor and the bot still TRADED it, grinding ~4.5h (16:01->20:45) rejecting nearly everything for 'HP weak macro' to scrape a +$0.28 win on a 0.10% target, then doing the same for Normal-2 -- 'wasted trading luck' and avoidable capital exposure (the later EIGEN trade lost -$2.18). FIX: a phase that the overshoot already fully covers is BANKED and SKIPPED, not traded. New _advance_session_phase() walks the 4-phase sequence (Normal-1 1.0 / HP-1 0.75 / Normal-2 0.5 / HP-2 0.25) and, at each transition, skips every upcoming phase whose FULL base target <= the accumulated overshoot credit (deducting each skipped base from the carry), then enters the first UNCOVERED phase; if the overshoot covers ALL remaining phases the session completes immediately (-> cooldown -> fresh session). Retro on log_c203: Normal-1 +2.02% -> HP-1 (0.75%) SKIPPED (carry 1.02->0.27%) -> straight to Normal-2 at 0.23% -- the bot banks the luck and stops grinding trivial-target phases. Replaces BOTH transitions (Normal->HP switch and the HP->cycle-advance) with the single skip-aware advance; per-phase re-anchoring, the C200 session machinery, and the C201 noise floor are UNCHANGED. ALSO logged this session (analysis, not yet fixed): the -$2.18 EIGEN loss was a BAD-TICK stop -- bought @0.2896, the hard stop 'filled' @0.2801 (-3.28%) 33s later, but the real EIGEN 15m candle low was only -0.4% and it ran +3.2%; an anomalous real-time tick (slipping the -5.5% stop to a -9.84% exit, blowing past the session cap) closed a trade the market never really moved against. A stop-confirmation / bad-tick guard is the recommended next fix. C203 ride-mode correctly did NOT fire (the tape was choppy/neutral, not trending) -- its fail-safe worked. Compile-clean; phase-skip simulated across overshoot magnitudes (skip-one / skip-to-complete / no-skip). NO change to entries, exits, sizing, or the loss cap."),
            ("C203", "RIDE STRONG TRENDS -- profit-capture could not let a winner run (from log_c202: 2 sessions, the active one 5 longs 2W/3L net -$1.54 = -3.1% in a BULLISH tape R=+0.68). Forensic+chart audit of every trade: the losses were NOT a direction problem (the longs were WITH the macro) -- they were (a) the bot capturing a fraction of every trend then quitting, and (b) two budget-strangled wick-outs. EPIC ran +9.4% price but POSITION_CAPTURE (C56/C104, the 1.5xPRU individual take-profit) banked it at +2.0% price (+$0.96 of a move that was worth ~$4-5); EIGEN ran +4.4% but EARLY_PEAK_CAPTURE banked it at a 33% pullback (+$0.22); VELVET was stopped at -2.0% within ONE MINUTE (a wick) then went +3.6%; ALICE was a deep -6.7% shakeout (stop defensible) that then ran +12.3%; only SLX (-7.7%) was a genuine wrong-side fall. The decisive lever: the C92 regime cross-talk TIGHTENS giveback when the macro opposes but never WIDENS when a strong trend supports the trade, and the 1.5xPRU hard capture is regime-blind -- so in a strong uptrend the bot scalps +2% and exits while the move runs +9%. FIX (symmetric to the existing tighten, relativistic, bounded): a RIDE MODE gated on with-trend STRENGTH (macro_dir x side > 0.30, since the regime persistence score 0.58 understated the +0.68-directional tape) AND a non-ranging live regime (>=0.45) AND regime-not-turning, which scales the individual-capture multiple 1.5 -> up to 3.0xPRU and the EARLY_PEAK_CAPTURE giveback tolerance 30% -> up to 48%, both proportional to trend strength. The hard stop and PEAK_FLOOR (breakeven exit if a peaked trade fully reverses) are UNCHANGED, so riding can only convert a small win into a larger one or give peak gains back toward breakeven -- it can NEVER turn a winner into a loser. Retro on log_c202 at the session regime: EPIC captures ~2-2.7xPRU instead of 1.5 and EIGEN rides past its 33% pullback -- EPIC alone re-rated to ~+$2-4 flips the session positive. DELIBERATELY NOT shipped: the auto-flip-to-short (still N<10 on the C202 missed-reversal log -- only 1 fired this session, BTC R:R 1.13) and the wick-out SIZING fix (size down so a noise-clearing stop fits the budget -- VELVET/ALICE), both flagged for the next pass. Compile-clean; ride params unit-checked across regime scores. NO change to entries, sizing, the hard stop, the C201 noise floor, or the C200 session machinery."),
            ("C202", "DIRECTIONAL-DIVERSITY DIAGNOSIS + missed-short transparency (from full log_c199 audit, user-flagged: trade/analysis conversion too low + does a blocked long imply a short). FINDINGS (confirmed, not a bug): (1) the log is mechanically HEALTHY -- 0 exceptions/tracebacks/silent-failures across 9757 lines; (2) the screen->trade funnel is 649 markets -> 163 volume-qualified -> top-30 by predictive rank (freshness+projected+geometric) -> analysed, and the ~1-candidate-per-scan conversion is MOSTLY justified filtering: poor reward:risk (target vs ~2xATR stop), C184 ATR-too-high vetoes, structural/micro-exhaustion, flat-projection -- all correct; (3) the REAL gap is DIRECTIONAL SKEW -- the session opened 7 LONG : 1 SHORT in a BEARISH (80%-short) market, because direction is chosen by a technical-vote consensus (EMA etc.) that favours the strongest-momentum pairs as longs even when they are overbought in a down-market; (4) ANSWER to 'does a blocked long mean short is good': NO in general -- it depends ENTIRELY on the block reason. Flat-projection / ATR-too-high / ranging => the short is equally bad. ONLY a DIRECTIONAL block (overbought structural/absorption exhaustion + opposing CVD + supportive macro) with good short-side R:R warrants the short -- and even then exhaustion != guaranteed reversal. Chart-validated the 7 waited-on overbought longs: shorts profited ONLY at SEVERE extremes (WLD RSI86 +3.0% MFE, ENA RSI82 +2.35%, ONDO +1.59%); moderate (DOGE/BNB RSI73-74) were flat/negative, so the bot's 'absorption -> wait' was CORRECT there. CHANGE THIS VERSION (safe, additive, logging-only -- NO behaviour change): the absorption-at-extreme branch now LOGS the would-be reversal trade (opposite side, its target, ~2xATR stop, R:R, and macro-agreement) whenever absorption is SEVERE (|real_cvd|>=0.50 and RSI>=78 long / <=22 short), tagged 'C202 tracking missed-reversal edge'. This measures the missed-short edge across live sessions -- the same validate-before-enable discipline used on the C199 boost -- before any actual auto-flip is enabled. The structural fix (make the DIRECTION VOTE holistic: add real-CVD + RSI-extreme-reversion + macro as votes so overbought-in-a-downtrend pairs vote SHORT at source, with a coherent short-side score) is DESIGNED but deliberately NOT shipped on N=7 -- it changes every pair's direction and needs its own validation pass. Spelling/eaten-words in the on-device console = a Pydroid3/Android terminal emoji/em-dash column-width rendering artifact; the saved .log file is clean UTF-8 (verified) -- not a code bug. Compile-clean; NO change to entries, exits, sizing, gates, the C200 session machinery, or the C201 noise floor."),
            ("C201", "TP/SL ASYMMETRY -- NOISE-CLEARING HARD-STOP FLOOR + C199 boost validation (from log_c199: 8 trades 5W/3L net -$0.60). Kelly proof the session was unprofitable purely on R:R: W=0.62, avg win ~+$0.30 / avg loss ~-$0.70 -> R=0.43 -> f*=0.62-0.38/0.43 = -0.26 (NEGATIVE edge). Forensics: 2 of the 3 losses (SYN short, MET long) were WICK-OUTS -- the position was directionally right (SYN ended -1.8% for the short, MET +0.5%) but a brief ~0.8x-ATR adverse swing tripped the hard stop, which had been strangled to -6.6/-6.3% PnL by the C174 budget bound -- INSIDE the pair's single-candle range. price_stop = _max_loss_pct/leverage and PRU = ATR% x leverage, so the budget bound (as tight as ~1.25% early-day) put the stop at <1x-ATR in price on volatile pairs. FIX: a NOISE-CLEARING FLOOR -- the final stop must be at least 1.30 x PRU in PnL (= 1.30 x ATR in price), so a single candle cannot eject a correct position. It ONLY widens a stop the budget strangled below noise (calm pairs unaffected), is bounded ABOVE by the C52 wave_cap so it cannot run away, and a pair too volatile to be stopped within that cap is already vetoed at entry by C184; the floor is ALSO bounded by 2x the C174 budget stop (which is HALF the remaining budget, so 2x = the full remaining = the session-cap boundary), so a single noise-widened stop brings equity AT MOST to the 2.5% cap, never through it (unit-verified across calm/volatile/tight-budget cases: SYN -6.6->-10.2% = 1.94% equity; the extreme ATR-5%/near-exhausted-budget case is bounded to exactly the cap). Retro-applied to log_c199: SYN at -6.6% (0.84x-ATR) would NOT have stopped (new floor ~-10.2% = 1.3x-ATR), and both wick-outs would have ridden to their recovery -- flipping ~2 losses toward the small wins they should have been. C199 VALIDATION (promised before any scale-up): the boost's CONFIRM signature is NOT reliable -- of 9 confirmed pairs, 3 continued / 5 reversed / 1 flat over the next 45min (BSB +2.2% then -16.9%). So the boost is NOT scaled; instead it is TIGHTENED to cut false positives: CVD-confirm threshold 0.15->0.25, an OI-strength>=0.30 requirement added, and the boost cap lowered 1.25->1.18. The exhaustion BLOCK side -- validated correct last session (RE/SYN/XPL all fell after being blocked) -- is left fully intact. Compile-clean; the noise-floor math is unit-checked on the SYN/MET cases and confirmed bounded by wave_cap and the session cap. NO change to entries, sizing, the climax veto, or the C200 session machinery."),
            ("C200", "SESSION STATE-MACHINE REWORK (user-specified, from log_c199 -- the 13h session 18:21->07:12 that 'reached Normal Cycle 2 at ~$49'). ROOT CAUSE: at calendar midnight check_new_day() fired mode_mgr.reset(current_equity), re-anchoring the target/cap baseline MID-SESSION from $50.00 down to $49.06. That dropped the Normal-1 bar from 1% of $50.00 ($50.50) to 1% of $49.06 ($49.55), so BTW pushing equity to $49.96 printed a FALSE 'NORMAL TARGET ACHIEVED 1.77%' even though $49.96 is still below the true $50.00 start -- then it advanced through HP and into Cycle 2. The goalposts moved at midnight. USER SPEC now implemented: a SESSION = 4 phases (Normal-1 1% / HP-1 0.75% / Normal-2 0.5% / HP-2 0.25%, each of THAT phase's own start equity, overshoot carrying forward); a session has NO time limit and runs all 4 phases to completion, spanning midnight freely with NO reset and NO re-anchor; ONE equity baseline and ONE 2.5% loss cap for the whole session; after the 4th phase concludes (achieved OR HP-failed) the bot waits min(now+4h, next midnight) then begins a FRESH session (re-anchored equity + cap + cycle plan). CHANGES: (1) removed the midnight mode_mgr.reset (the bug) -- check_new_day still logs housekeeping but never resets targets/cap/cycles; (2) check_new_day no longer resets the Portfolio session at midnight (it persists across midnight, re-anchored only at a new trading session); (3) deleted the '>=4h/>=3h left in the calendar day' gates that previously blocked Cycle-2 and paused-for-day -- Cycle 2 now always starts (no time limit); (4) new start_session_cooldown() replaces pause_until_tomorrow after the 4th phase, setting pause_until=min(+4h, next midnight) and a _pending_new_session flag; (5) new begin_new_session() re-anchors normal_start_equity, hp_start_equity, _day_start_equity (cap), _session_cycles=0, _overshoot_credit=0, hp_attempts=0; (6) the main loop spawns the fresh session when the cooldown elapses; (7) _day_start_equity and _pending_new_session now persist to the mode file so a mid-session restart keeps its baseline. Per-phase re-anchoring (each phase targets its own start equity) and the overshoot cascade are UNCHANGED. Retro-checked vs log_c199: under C200 the midnight reset does not fire, Normal-1 stays anchored to $50.00 (bar $50.50), BTW at $49.96 would NOT have printed target-achieved, and the session would have kept grinding Cycle 1 on the true baseline. Compile-clean; state-machine simulation verifies session->4 phases->cooldown(min 4h/midnight)->fresh session, and a mid-session midnight crossing with no reset. NO change to entries, exits, sizing, the C185 climax veto, or the C199 order-flow overlay."),
            ("C199", "ORDER-FLOW CONTINUATION/EXHAUSTION OVERLAY (user-requested leading-indicator engine; log_c198: 1 trade, WLD long -$0.18; the market was a stock-picker tape -- BTC/ETH flat (R=+0.02) but BTW +26%, SYN +37%, VELVET +33%, BEAT +11% moving). The bot SCREENED every mover but its overbought ensemble scored them ~0.04 and blocked entry. Chart truth: most reversed (SYN -5%, BEAT -17%, RE -5% -> correctly avoided) but BTW continued +12.9% (missed). The decisive finding: BTW (+12.9%) and BEAT (-16.8%) were INDISTINGUISHABLE from price alone -- both non-turning up-movers, and the bot scored the winner LOWER (BTW 0.04 vs BEAT 0.28) -- so looser gates would catch BEAT first. The ONLY ex-ante separator is LEADING ORDER FLOW: live-verified that Bitget exposes per-pair OI (open-interest endpoint), real CVD (side-tagged /fills), funding, and order-book depth for ALL alts (only the aggregated L/S account ratio is gappy for small alts -> 40054). FIX: a new overlay just before the low_score gate, gated to plausible directional movers (score>=0.25, with-trend, X<1.8 so the C185 climax veto is never overridden). It reads OI divergence (get_oi_divergence: strong_trend/weak_rally/bearish_buildup/capitulation) + the already-fetched real CVD delta and: (a) BOOSTS a candidate when OI AND CVD jointly confirm continuation [strength-scaled, capped x1.25 -- cannot resurrect a dead 0.04 pair, so BTW stays correctly dead; it lifts BORDERLINE confirmed continuations over the line]; (b) BLOCKS on DOUBLE exhaustion (OI and CVD both distribute = unambiguous blow-off -- a pure safety ADD that makes the bot stricter, not looser, on blow-offs); (c) applies a graded x0.75 on single-signal divergence. CVD works from scan 1 (no history); OI warms up over a few scans, so the safety penalty is immediate and the boost engages as OI history fills. HONEST SCOPE & VERIFICATION: this sharpens the MARGIN (borderline continuations + blow-off protection); it deliberately does NOT chase extended legs (that is the overfit trap C190 rejected). Order-flow efficacy CANNOT be retro-tested (OI/CVD are real-time-only), so the boost is intentionally conservative pending FORWARD validation in live logs -- once the OI+CVD continuation signature is shown to precede continuation (and the exhaust signature to precede reversal), the boost cap can be scaled up data-driven in C200+. Compile-clean; functional cases proven (confirm->boost, double-exhaust->block, single->penalty, <0.25 untouched, X>=1.8 untouched); live OI+CVD inputs verified real on current Bitget data. NO change to exits, sizing, or the climax veto."),
            ("C198", "OBSERVABILITY (user XPL/XLM screenshot question from log_c197): why was XPL screened #4 in Step-1 at 10:31 but never analyzed that cycle, then opened the next cycle 7min later -- did its prediction change? NO. XPL WON a Normal short at 09:31:34; the bot was in HP mode continuously after (HP target 0.75% never hit), so the re-entry cooldown was max(30,60)=60min (C125-F43), expiring 10:31:34 -- and the Step-1 scan ran at 10:31:28, SIX SECONDS before expiry. So XPL was on cooldown and silently skipped from Step-3 (the open/cooldown `continue` at the top of the scan loop logs nothing), which is why the cycle showed 29 analyzed from a top-30 and XPL had no reason line. By the 10:37:49 cycle the cooldown had expired (same 15m candle, so 29 verdicts were cache-reused and only XPL was freshly analyzed -> 1 analyzed +29 cached), it scored 0.821 and opened SHORT @0.0933 -- the SAME prediction, gated 7min earlier by a 60-min timer, not a changed forecast. (Chart truth: that re-entry then bounced +2.06% and was cut by STAGNANT_LOSS at -$0.36 -- a poor re-short of an exhausting oversold leg, well contained.) FIX: the old Filtered-N line sat in Step 5 and never fired when 0 passed; now Step 3 logs each screened pair skipped on re-entry cooldown WITH the minutes remaining, so a screened-but-unanalyzed pair is never a mystery. Pure observability -- no entry/exit behavior changes. (Same-session DRI/DSI sign-convention audit: CORRECT -- DRI negative=low-reversal=good, 0=neutral (|dri|<0.03 dead-zoned), positive=reversal building (0.30 exit / 0.50 hard); DSI=-(projected)=positive-sustains, opposite sign; gap=DSI-DRI, positive=healthy. Candle-anatomy (hammer/shooting-star/wick-rejection/micro-exhaustion) and the multi-TF weighting (15m highest, 1m/3m down-weighted, direction from 1h/4h/12h resultant) verified sound. DRI thresholds deliberately NOT retuned on one XPL loss -- C190 anti-overfit discipline.)"),
            ("C197", "MODE-TARGET LEDGER FIX from log_c195 (clean $50.00 Cycle-1 start, yet Normal C1 target printed 0.70% not 1.00% and HP C1 0.73%). ROOT CAUSE: reset() zeroes the overshoot ledger only INSIDE the `_session_cycles != 0` branch, so a fresh process start with _session_cycles loaded as 0 but a non-zero _overshoot_credit persisted from a prior session inherited that stale 0.30% credit and applied it against Cycle-1 Normal (1.00% base - 0.30% = 0.70%). The cycle-counter reset and the ledger reset are separate concerns that were wrongly coupled. FIX: on any fresh day-start (process restart, _day_start_equity was None) that is NOT a mid-HP crash-recovery resume (_recent_hp guard preserved), clear _overshoot_credit to 0 so Cycle-1 Normal targets a clean 1.00% of its starting equity per spec. Within-session mode-to-mode carry and the cross-mode cascade (Normal->HP->Normal2->HP2, leftover credit cascading to the mode after next when it exceeds the next mode full target) are UNCHANGED -- reset() is not called on within-session cycle transitions (_day_start_equity is set, so the day-start block is skipped). Schedule confirmed correct: Normal C1 1.0% / HP C1 0.75% / Normal C2 0.5% / HP C2 0.25%, each of the start equity of THAT cycle."),
            ("C195", "SCANNER UNIVERSE FIX from log_c194 (1 trade in 3.5h, then 0 viable for 3h while the Bitget Gainers board showed ESPORTS +108%, SYN +69%, BSB +29%, MAGMA/FOLKS/HOME/TAG/US all +23-29%). ROOT CAUSE: get_all_tickers() truncated the market list to [:200] of 643 active USDT swaps, so 443 pairs were NEVER fetched, screened or scored. The Bitget contract ordering puts established coins in the first ~200 and NEW LISTINGS at idx 300-650 -- i.e. the truncation was biased to hide exactly the fresh, explosive movers the predictive engine exists to catch. Verified via live API: ESPORTS idx 588 ($56M vol), SYN 364, BSB 293, US 311, TAG 419, ATU 444, HOME 465, FOLKS 555, MAGMA 559, UNITAS 613 -- all beyond the cut; only TAC (64) and ARC (40) were visible (ARC then volume-filtered). Every scan reported the SAME 52 volume-passing pairs because it was always the SAME stale 200. F1: fetch the FULL universe -- list(self.markets.keys()) with no slice. bitget fetch_tickers hits the bulk /tickers endpoint ONCE regardless of list length (no per-symbol calls), so cost is unchanged (~1s); Phase-3 OHLCV is still capped at the top-38 buffer. Effect: candidate pool ~52 -> ~120, and new-listing momentum is now eligible for the same DRI/DSI screening as everything else. NOTE: visibility fix only -- it does NOT force entries; once seen, ESPORTS-type parabolas still face the C185 climax/exhaustion vetoes and may still be skipped or shorted. KNOWN NEXT STEP (left isolated for C196): Phase-2 current_score normalizes volume against BTC/ETH absolute volume (vol_ratio=vol/max_vol), so every alt scores ~0 on the 0.40 volume + 0.35 freshness terms and is ranked almost purely on raw 24h % -- a log-scaled or percentile volume term would rank mid-cap movers on their own cohort, per Principle 1."),
            ("C194", "DEVELOPING-LEG dead-zone fix from log_c193 (ZERO trades in 3.6h while FARTCOIN ran +5.1%, HYPE +3.9%, XLM +2.7%). IST chart audit confirmed the market was MIXED, not flat — majors quiet (BTC +1.5%) but several alts moved. Root cause: the room-to-resistance target throttled these movers to a 0.0-1.1% target → poor_RR blocked, and the C191 breakout re-projection FAILED to rescue them because its fresh-leg window (X<1.0) and macro gate (≥0.4) were too strict — XLM/FARTCOIN sat at X≈1.1, macro≈0.30: a DEVELOPING leg, past the fresh midpoint but FAR below the X≥1.8 exhaustion line. They fell into a dead-zone (not fresh enough to re-project, not spent enough to block, room-throttled to a losing RR). F1: extend the re-projection window to the developing leg — X<1.5 AND X2<1.5 (still strictly below the 1.8 exhaustion floor so EDGE/COAI blow-offs stay blocked by exhaustion), macro ≥0.25, room ≤0.28. Verified: XLM re-projects target 1.11→1.80% (RR 0.49→0.75), FARTCOIN 1.02→1.63% (RR 0.75), both survive the C184 equity cap (eq-risk 4.3-4.8% at 2x). 6/6 separation: XLM/FARTCOIN qualify; HYPE (no macro, room 0.56), the X≥1.8 disasters, and a borderline X=1.7 blow-off all stay excluded. HONEST TRADE-OFF (retro on real data): the newly-allowed entries are a MIX — FARTCOIN +3.1%/+1.7%, EPIC +2.0% are wins, XLM +1.4% marginal, one XLM entry was a -2.2% loss-risk. This is a CONSCIOUS choice: the bot was taking ZERO trades and missing +5% movers; a controlled increase in activity with the C184 cap (-9% max) + stop bounding the downside and the C193 breakout profile (looser trail) letting winners run is the right direction for a too-passive bot. NOTE: C193's management profile was NOT the cause of zero trades (it only touches exits); this was a pre-existing entry dead-zone surfaced by a mixed-but-quiet tape."),
            ("C193", "STRATEGY-DIFFERENTIATED MANAGEMENT PROFILE (deepening Principle 3, per user request: relativistic, no absolutes, handles trajectory change + mixed profiles). New Position._strategy_mgmt_profile() returns four dimensionless MULTIPLIERS — trail_mult (giveback tolerance), target_mult, patience_mult (stagnant/DSI timer), stop_mult — that reshape the exit machinery per the position's strategy CHARACTER. (1) RELATIVISTIC: every archetype is multipliers on PRU/ATR; a 0.2%-ATR and an 8%-ATR pair are treated identically scaled to their own volatility; no absolute %/$ anywhere. (2) MIXED PROFILES: rather than hard-bucketing, the archetypes are BLENDED by how strongly the position currently matches trend-ness vs reversal-ness (from live macro alignment + continuation health), so a 60/40 breakout/momentum pair gets an interpolated profile. (3) TRAJECTORY CHANGE: the blend weights are recomputed every tick from LIVE signals and EMA-migrated (α=0.25, ~4 ticks), so a breakout that morphs into a fading reversal tightens its OWN trail/patience dynamically with no hard switch — verified migrating trail 1.27→1.14 over 6 ticks. Archetypes: breakout (trail 1.35/let-run) & trend_following (1.20) loosen the trail and lengthen the stagnant timer to ride runners; divergence (0.75)/funding_reversal (0.70)/range (0.70) tighten both to bank reversals fast; momentum (1.00) neutral; deep-peak extension (relativistic via peak_in_PRU) always pulls any profile toward banking. Wired into the C30 giveback-threshold engine (trail_mult, clamped so it can't invert peak-depth ordering) and the C144 stagnant timer (patience_mult, floored 6min). Faithful backtest V_reversal +$1.15 = C192 (no regression — multipliers cluster near 1.0, diverging only when character is clear). NOTE: target_mult/stop_mult are computed and exposed but currently advisory; next step is wiring target_mult into the re-projection and stop_mult into the REL_HARD_STOP tolerance."),
            ("C192", "RELATIVISTIC-PRINCIPLE audit + fix (user asked: is the bot truly (1) self-relative and (2) regime-relative, jointly driving a dynamic projective strategy?). Audit verdict (RELATIVISTIC_AUDIT.md): P1 self-relative is genuinely followed in the quantitative core — N52 leg-capacity is the pair OWN p70 of completed legs, projection = own momentum×own ATR, stops/targets ATR-relative, DRI/DSI per-position baselines; P2 regime-relative is genuinely followed INCLUDING dynamic per-pair signal RE-WEIGHTING (Hurst<0.45 → amplify reversion/dampen momentum; strong 4h trend → boost trend-agreeing signals, dampen fighting ones, inject synthetic trend signal); P3 entry/score/targets jointly driven and projective. F1 fixes the one clear P1 LEAK found: trend_stage classification used ABSOLUTE cutoffs (range = ret_4h<0.5% AND ret_1h<0.3%; early needs ret_1h>1.0%) — a 4%-ATR coin and a 0.4%-ATR coin faced the same bar, so a quiet high-vol coin mislabelled 'range' and a moving low-vol coin mislabelled trending. Now relativised to the pair's OWN ATR: range = 4h<2×ATR AND 1h<1×ATR (floored at the old absolutes); early = ret_1h>max(1.0, ATR%). Verified across BTC (ATR 0.20%) → BEAT (ATR 8.01%): each gets a stage and projection on its OWN scale. KNOWN REMAINING GAP (documented, not yet changed): the chosen strategy LABEL (momentum/breakout/reversal/…) does not yet produce a differentiated position-MANAGEMENT profile — a breakout and a reversal are managed by the same DRI/DSI+trail+stop. That is the highest-value next deepening of P3 (breakout→let-run/wider trail; reversal→tighter target)."),
            ("C191", "MISSED-WINNER fix from log_c190 (8.7h, 5 trades 4W/1L NET +$1.18, 80% WR — strong session, but IST chart audit found a SYSTEMATIC miss). The poor_RR gate (451 blocks, the dominant category) blocked EPIC — the session's top scorer (0.76-1.03, macro +1.0, fresh leg X=0.46/X2=0.59, prob 0.71) — at poor_RR 0.49 TWICE, and it then ran +14.1% and +14.2% with only -1.8% adverse (RR 7.8/8.1). Also missed USELESS +7.9% (RR 99), ALLO +5.2%. ROOT CAUSE: C187's breakout re-projection HAD qualified EPIC (own_breakout=True) but the target was capped at min(3.0%, 1.5×ATR) — and for high-ATR pairs (EPIC ATR 3.04%) the 3.0% cap makes RR=3.0/(2×3.04)=0.49 MATHEMATICALLY GUARANTEED to fail the 0.5 floor. The cap that prevents over-projection on low-ATR pairs DEFEATS the re-projection on high-ATR pairs — exactly the pairs with the biggest moves. SECOND failure: @13:30 EPIC's room was EXACTLY 0.20, excluded by the strict <0.20. F1 (two parts): (a) re-projection target cap now scales — a fresh breakout may target up to 0.55×stop (so RR can clear 0.5) but never beyond the measured 1.5×ATR extension; (b) room threshold widened 0.20→0.25. EPIC now passes both points (target 2.71→3.35%, RR 0.49→0.55). 5/5 separation verified: EDGE/COAI disaster classes stay blocked by the climax veto (X≥1.8, independent of RR), genuinely-bad low-RR and weak-macro setups still block. The COAI loss (-$0.60, stopped on a -2.2% dip then ran +7.1%) was noise bounded by the C184 cap — stop logic deliberately untouched (4W/1L is healthy)."),
            ("C190", "Analysis of log_c189 (66min, ZERO trades, C189) — user asked: missed winners? + why does Step 3 analyze 30/3/1 pairs? FINDINGS: (1) STEP 3 PAIR-COUNT is EXPECTED — the C188 15m-bucket memoization means the FIRST scan in each 15m candle analyzes all ~30 pairs, but later scans within the SAME candle reuse cached verdicts for already-judged pairs (forming-candle data unchanged), showing '3 analyzed' or '1 analyzed'; zero is possible if all are cache-reused/screened. The rejection-reason counters still tally the cache-reused pairs, which made 'analyzed' look inconsistent. F1 logs '(+N cached)' to clarify. (2) MISSED WINNERS (IST-verified per protocol): YES some — XLM long blocked poor_RR 0.29 then ran +6.9% (RR 10.3); BANANAS31 long blocked R-EXTREME-confirm then +3.3%; 1000BONK +2.2%. BUT after rigorous analysis these are DEFENSIBLE blocks, NOT fixed: XLM had N52 X=3.13 (leg 213% past fuel cap) in a macro=+1.0 trend — from available signals this is INDISTINGUISHABLE from a blow-off top that reverses (the exact C183/C185 disaster class the exhaustion gate exists to catch); relaxing exhaustion to catch it (even to X-thresh 1.8) still fails X=3.13 and would reopen -8.9%-type losses. BANANAS31 had 'already moved +10.6%' at near-zero conviction in an extreme-R market — blocking a chase-into-extreme is correct. The 21:02 BANANAS31 was correctly blocked by the C184 equity cap (ATR 1.6%→10% equity risk). Base-rate check of exhausted-blocked legs: 1 reversed / 2 ran (too small to overturn the gate). DECISION: do NOT loosen exhaustion/confirm gates — missing some runners is the cost of avoiding larger reversals; chasing them overfits to lucky outcomes. Honest conclusion: the bot's selectivity is working as designed; in a mild-up tape (BTC +0.5%/ETH +0.9%) it correctly stayed flat rather than chase extended legs."),
            ("C189", "Three fixes from log2 (22-min C187 session, 2W/0L, user-flagged). F1 SAME-DAY-RESTART CYCLE DESYNC (the 'big error'): the bot restarted mid-day at 17:19 IST, freshly set Day-start equity $50 (because _day_start_equity was None in the new process) BUT loaded _session_cycles=1 from disk — so it reset for EQUITY/target purposes yet CONTINUED for cycle-counting, labelling the first Normal 'Cycle 2' and, after one Normal+HP, hitting the <2 ceiling → paused for the day, losing a whole cycle. Fix: when a fresh day-start equity is set (process restart, _day_start_equity None) and _session_cycles persisted >0, reset the counter to Cycle 1 and zero the overshoot ledger — GUARDED exactly like the midnight reset (NOT if HP is active/cooling, so a genuine mid-HP crash-recovery resumes its cycle). F2 DOUBLE-PERCENT LOG CORRUPTION ('spelling errors'): the live CLIMAX log f-string used a doubled percent sign (renders literal double-percent in an f-string, unlike %-format) — fixed to single, and swept the _CHANGELOG tuples (written via f.write(f-string)) for 75 more doubled-percent fixes. F4 STATE-RELOAD EXIT GAP: 'Load Previous State' restored a position's identity but NOT its exit machinery — _planned_target, _pru, locked dri/dsi baselines, dsi_values, and _budget_stop_pct were never persisted, so a position reloaded after a restart silently lost its take-profit, PRU scaling, DSI exits, and budget stop (mismanaged live position). Now all 7 exit-critical fields are saved and restored (round-trip verified). F3 SCAN CLUTTER: C187's broadened breakout re-projection fires on most pairs in a trending tape (log2's market was uniformly RSI 74-97 overbought) — the per-pair '🔓 re-projected' line demoted to debug; the target change still applies, final pass/block reasons stay at info. NOTE: the IST re-verification (C188) showed re-projection over-fires harmlessly (climax/exhaustion gates catch the spent legs), so F3 is cosmetic; the entry logic is unchanged."),
            ("C188", "Timezone-rigor correction + log-spam fix + 1s-monitor confirmation (user-flagged). (1) TIMEZONE: re-verified all log_c186 chart findings in IST (log timestamps are IST=UTC+5:30; Bitget API epochs are UTC) using the last-SETTLED-close as the bot's true current_price. This CORRECTED an overstatement in C187: USELESS was +2.96% favorable but -2.51% adverse first (real RR 1.18, NOT the clean +5.3%/-0.3% I claimed from a boundary-sliced reference). The C187 breakout re-projection stays (well-guarded, 7/7 separation, harmless) but its evidence was weaker than stated. The IST re-check also showed the CLIMAX veto (C185) is the imperfect gate: it correctly blocked DASH (-2.6% adv) and PENDLE (faded) but missed TIA (+2.4%, -0.14% adv) and JUP (RR 1.71) — yet TIA and DASH are near-IDENTICAL at entry (macro +0.41/+0.61, X2 1.88/1.94, forecast -0.37% both) with OPPOSITE outcomes, i.e. genuinely coin-flip from available signals. Deliberately NOT adding another filter (would overfit 4 points); the veto avoids -2.6% losses at the cost of +2% misses, net-reasonable, and C184 bounds either error. (2) C92 RESULTANT-FLIP SPAM: the warning logged 31× with identical scan=+0.04→live=-0.40 because a persistent disagreement re-fired each regime refresh — now EDGE-TRIGGERED (logs only on transition into flipped), flag still updates every cycle. (3) MONITORING confirmed every 1.0s (POSITION_CHECK_INTERVAL=1.0, DRI gate ≥1s); the ~26s flip spacing was the spam artifact, not a monitor delay — banner clarified."),
            ("C187", "MISSED-OPPORTUNITY fix from log_c186 (8.7h, 2 trades 2W/0L +$0.95 — clean but the user asked: did it miss winners? YES). Empirical chart audit of the strongest REJECTED candidates: climax blocks were mostly correct/marginal (JUP/TIA/IP offered only +1.5-1.6% with -1 to -1.9% adverse first; PENDLE short faded — block correct), BUT the poor_RR gate (618 blocks, the largest funnel category) MISSED real winners — most starkly USELESS long: blocked at RR 0.34 (target 1.35% vs stop 3.97%), it then ran +5.3% with only -0.3% adverse. Root cause: USELESS was an EARLY-stage breakout (own _macro_dir +0.59 aligned, N52 X=0.46 fresh leg + decel, trend_stage 'early') but its target was THROTTLED to 0.68×ATR by _long_room=0.09 ('near resistance') — and the C172-F1 breakout re-projection missed it because (a) it keyed on the MARKET-wide resultant not the PAIR's own macro, and (b) it only fired at target<0.3% absolute, not target-small-vs-ATR. F1 BROADENED BREAKOUT RE-PROJECTION: also re-project the target to 1.5×ATR when the entry is the pair's OWN aligned (macro·dir≥0.4), non-exhausted (X<1.0 AND X2<1.2), throttled (target<1.2×ATR), low-room (<0.20) breakout — room-to-resistance is the wrong cap for a breakout. USELESS retro: target 1.35%→2.98%, RR 0.34→0.75 → PASSES (catches the +5.3% winner). 7/7 separation verified: the C183 disaster class (EDGE X=2.24, COAI counter-trend), all climax/spent legs, and non-breakouts are EXCLUDED by the four-guard AND — recovers the winner without reopening any prior wound."),
            ("C186", "RR-GATE CONVICTION EXEMPTION from log_c185x3 (3 sessions; the disastrous one: 3 trades 0W/3L -$0.95 = -1.9%, ALL slow STAGNANT_LOSS deaths) — while the broad market RALLIED +2.7% BTC / +3.3% ETH. Forensic: the C183-F3 reward:risk gate (RR = target/(2×ATR)) is mechanically an ATR FILTER — it favours low-ATR pairs (small stop denominator) and penalises higher-conviction movers. The bot REJECTED its best candidates (nearest-miss score 0.85-1.005, conf 0.83-0.92) for poor_RR, leaving only score-0.50 dregs (JASMY/SLX, EQI 0.20-0.29, 'FEEDBACK NEUTRAL') as the lone viable pick — longs that didn't participate in the rally and bled to the stagnant timer. F1 CONVICTION EXEMPTION: a score≥0.80 entry whose OWN projector rates continuation_prob≥0.62 earns a relaxed 0.35 RR floor (logged ⚖️ exemption); the strict 0.5 floor still applies to everything else, so the EDGE/COAI/2Z disaster class (score ~0.55, prob ~0.55, RR 0.25) STAYS blocked and the C184 equity cap still bounds per-trade loss. Retro-verified: the 0.85-1.0 leaders (RR 0.39-0.47) now pass and would outrank the dregs in selection; disaster class still blocked. NOTE: the lone-marginal-candidate problem (taking a 0.50 when it is genuinely the only viable) was deliberately NOT over-filtered — surfacing the wrongly-excluded leaders is the right lever, not tightening into near-total abstention."),
            ("C185", "CLIMAX VETO from backtest v2 (faithful exits via the REAL should_exit_dri; 8 auto-classified regime archetypes from ~20 days of real Bitget data, 3-4h windows). Faithful-exit finding: the bot loses systematically by entering at LEG CLIMAXES — the single largest loss in the sweep was a SHORT at COAI X=2.24 (down-leg 124% beyond its own p70 fuel cap) while the N52 next-candle forecast read +1.56% UP — shorting the exact capitulation bottom (-8.9%). The C175 'burning hot → ride the impulse' pass (correct for X just over 1.0) was extending to blow-off extremes. F1 CLIMAX VETO: a continuation entry is blocked when X≥1.8 on EITHER scale AND the N52 next-candle forecast opposes the trade direction by ≥0.30% — a blow-off/capitulation climax is not a rideable leg regardless of velocity. Retro-verified: blocks the -8.9% COAI climax short, spares the V-reversal long winner (X=0.70) and fresh-leg entries. NOTE (honest scope): the backtest also showed counter-trend losses with NO climax signature (fresh-leg shorts that simply failed, X<0.3, aligned forecast) — these are irreducible trade-level noise bounded by the C184 stop, deliberately NOT filtered to avoid overfitting. Backtest remains conservative on flow signals (live-only data → neutral) and cannot model real slippage/funding/sub-15m ticks."),
            ("C184", "BACKTEST-DRIVEN per-trade equity-risk cap (first multi-regime historical backtest: 5 regimes — flat-chop, the -$1.11 long-disaster, a V-reversal, a clean down-leg, and a mixed day — driving the REAL quick_scan_analysis + gates over historical Bitget candles). Finding: the C61 PRU-cap (2.0%) is DEFEATED by the MIN_LEVERAGE floor on high-ATR alts — EDGE at ATR 3.0% → int(2.0/3.0)=0 → floored to 2x → PRU stays 6% → hard stop (~2.2×PRU) ≈ -13-18% EQUITY on a SINGLE trade (the dominant faithful-exit loss; backtest showed EDGE -18.1%/-12.5%). F1 PER-TRADE EQUITY-RISK CAP: the hard stop's equity footprint (≈2.0×ATR×lev) must stay ≤9%; if exceeded, reduce leverage further, and if even MIN_LEVERAGE can't bound it (ATR ≳2.25% at 2x), VETO the entry — a pair that volatile cannot be stopped inside 9% without a noise-tight stop. Backtest impact (cap active across all 5 regimes): net -$2.65 → +$1.02, worst single trade -18.1% → -8.3%, high-ATR(>2.5%) entries 12 → 0, every faithful winner preserved (down-leg stayed +, 3W/0L). This bounds per-trade ruin — the key live-survivability property. NOTE: shorts (2W/0L) and the long-skew were verified REGIME-APPROPRIATE, not a bias bug; STAGNANT/PEAK proxy-exit losses in the harness are NOT code-faithful and were excluded from inference."),
            ("C183", "DISASTER fix-set from log_c182x2 (9 trades 3W/6L NET -$1.11 = -3.28% on HP equity; 4 of 6 losses were REL_HARD_STOP on LONGS). Forensic+chart root cause: the bot bought local tops on high-ATR alts that reversed on the VERY NEXT candle (EDGE next-bar -1.11%, COAI -2.49%, 2Z -0.10%) while the broad tape was flat-to-up (BTC +0.08%) and the R-blend read strongly bullish (+0.53..+0.60) — stale-R-in-whipsaw, individual pairs snapping while macro said up. THREE complementary fixes (defense in depth): F1 DUAL-THRESHOLD DRIFT ABORT — the C174-F4 0.8×ATR bar INVERTS on high-ATR pairs (COAI ATR 2.97% → 2.38% bar, so a -0.79% adverse signal→fill snap entered with only a margin trim → -$0.88). Abort = MIN(0.8×ATR, 0.75% absolute cap): a hard adverse snap aborts regardless of ATR (catches EDGE -1.11%, COAI -0.79%; spares BEAT -0.40%). F2 N52 EXHAUSTION COOLDOWN — EDGE was N52-blocked 3× (X=1.22) then ENTERED 22min later as its ATR ROSE 0.91→3.29% (more dangerous) once the zigzag re-anchored → -$0.77; a symbol+direction blocked for leg-exhaustion is now suppressed 20min. F3 REWARD:RISK RATIO gate (the dominant fix) — the C172-F1 re-projected target (1.5×ATR) was paired with a ~2×PRU hard stop, giving price-space RR of 0.14-0.25:1 on all four hard-stops (2Z 1.5% target vs 6.0% stop); continuation entries now require target ≥0.5×(2×ATR) price-space reward:risk. Retro: F3 alone blocks all 4 hard-stops (-$2.45) while passing BEAT#1 (+$0.94, RR 0.85) and the other 2 winners — session -$1.11 → ≈+$1.34."),
            ("C182", "Quiet-session refinement from a 2h log (21 scans, 1 trade, 0 monitor errors — C181 fix held). Chart truth: dead-flat tape (BTC +0.17%, ETH +0.29%, SOL +0.38% over 2h) and the 20 zero-trade scans were CORRECT abstention (blocked leg_exhausted longs TRUMP -0.35%/PENGU +0.69% went nowhere). The one trade, SHIB long, is the lesson: it scored pre-penalty 0.69 from capitulation=+1.0 at RSI 72 with projected_move=+0.0% and ATR at the 0.30% floor, earned the lenient 0.35 quality-floor on score ALONE, entered at 0.41, never moved >±0.25%, and bled -$0.31 to the stagnant timer — a position that should not have opened. F1 PROJECTION-GATED LENIENCY: the lenient 0.35/0.38 floors (which exist to rescue heavily-PENALIZED strong signals like QUBT/NMR) now also require |projected_move| ≥ 0.5×ATR; a static/flat-projection signal falls back to the strict 0.42 floor (SHIB's 0.41 would have failed). Orthogonal to C180-F1, which still lifts post-penalty score off the floor for genuinely-moving signals. Retro-verified: SHIB blocks, QUBT/NMR pass."),
            ("C181", "NameError fix exposed by C180-F4 (log: 'Monitor error ALLO: name price is not defined', ~60s cadence). The C48 PLANNED_TARGET exit block in should_exit_dri referenced bare `price` at 4 lines while the method parameter is `current_price` — so every monitor tick on any position carrying a _planned_target (C176-F1 revived this path) raised NameError, and because the exception unwound to the monitor's per-symbol try, the ENTIRE intelligent-exit cascade below that line (trailing TP, Ichimoku TK, DSI/DRI, budget stop) never executed for that position. Surfaced on ALLO (proxy-flow position) but latent for all. Fixed all 4 refs → current_price; the take-profit now actually fires. Verified by exercising the exact _hit_target branch live (clean), plus a whole-file AST sweep for used-but-unbound names across all 15 flagged methods — the price/current_price mismatch was the only real instance (others were nested-helper params or conditional imports). Atlas failure-pattern #9 (silent excepts in exits) + the C177 Config-integrity lesson both applied."),
            ("C180", "LIVE-TRADING TEMPLATE release. log_c179 (14 scans, 0 trades): chart truth vindicated abstention for the THIRD session running — ORDI long blocked at X=1.04 then fell -2.77%; BEAT long blocked at X=1.53 then crashed -12.46% before whipsawing; market drifted -0.9..-1.3% against a stale R=+0.27..+0.43 blend (murky transition, no edge). Template hardening: F1 GLOBAL PENALTY-STACK FLOOR ordering fix — the ⚖️ floor ran AFTER the low_score/vol_floor gates it should protect; QUBT (pre-pen 0.767, conf 0.901) was judged at 0.20 (-74% multiplicative crush). Score can never fall below 40% of its own pre-penalty value at any consuming gate (idempotent lifts before low_score and vol_floor). F2 MASTER BAR CAP: bar multipliers stack (TF-tension ×1.26, HP ×1.15, conviction ×1.25) — BEAT faced 0.6993236250000001; no effective bar may exceed 0.72, plus display rounding. F3 LIVE reduceOnly: closes pass reduce_only=True → params['reduceOnly'] in the live branch, so exits can never open/extend a position in live trading (paper ignores). F4 monitor-loop exceptions raised debug→warning (C165-class silence is lethal in live). Known-cosmetic (deliberately deferred): nearest-miss line can display the stale captured score; the live score appears in the gate's own ❌ line."),
            ("C179", "Forensic fix-set from log_c178 (1W/1L -$0.36 in 4h; chart-verified the final-hour mass blocks were CORRECT — USELESS topped +1.35% after refusal then faded, BANANAS31's short exit dodged a +10.7% moonshot by 4h, and the C174 budget stop cleanly capped APR at -2.5%). F1 pending-reason root cause: gate tracker updates used strict score-> against a best_rejected that already held THE SAME pair from the early capture → self-comparison false → 'pending' survived (USELESS q=0.978). Same-symbol clause added to all 9 update sites. F2 REAL-CVD ARBITRATION on the L/S flow veto: USELESS long vetoed at L/S R=-0.60 while its OWN /fills delta read +0.55 buyers — L/S aggregates are proxy-grade for alts (C158, roadmap #1); when real_cvd aligns with entry ≥0.40 the veto stands down (absorption/late-leg/N52 layers still guard). F3 TR-ATR primary for Gate-4 reprojection + planned-target (close-to-close atr_pct floors at 0.30% on based-out pairs → USELESS targets undersized to the 0.5% floor). F4 decel refinement: a pause candle now flips decel only when burn has also dropped below 0.90 of the leg's own mean — vel≥0.90 pauses are breaths, not exhaustion (the USELESS vel=0.76 block itself stays, and charts proved it RIGHT: +1.35% then fade; the fix targets the contradiction class where a full-burn leg got 'DECELERATING' from one flat candle)."),
            ("C178", "OVERSHOOT CARRY-FORWARD (user spec): when any cycle overshoots its target, the surplus becomes a credit that proportionally reduces subsequent cycles' effective targets (floor 0.10%/cycle; leftover cascades), so the day converges to the planned ~2.5% total regardless of how unevenly cycles deliver it. Base schedule (N 1.0/0.5, HP 0.75/0.25 of each cycle's start equity) untouched — only the EFFECTIVE target adjusts; e.g. log_c175's N1 +1.56% would set HP1 to 0.75-0.56=0.19%. Implemented as ModeManager.effective_cycle_target()/settle_cycle_overshoot() with a ♻️ ledger log; settle runs BEFORE mode switch so the HP banner already shows the carry-reduced target. Persistence: _session_cycles (previously NOT saved — a mid-day restart reset targets to cycle-1!) and _overshoot_credit now in the mode file; new-day reset zeroes the ledger."),
            ("C177", "CYCLE-TARGET SCHEDULE restored to user spec: Normal C1 = 1.0%, HP C1 = 0.75%, Normal C2 = 0.5%, HP C2 = 0.25% — each of THAT cycle's own starting equity. log_c175 evidence: HP1 ran at 0.25% (Gnedenko squeeze: max(0.25, 1.75-cap minus Normal's banked 1.56)), C2 printed 0.3752%/0.18% from (2.50-achieved)×0.67 arithmetic — the C142 dynamic day-cap ladder silently overrode the C138-F74 design at every cycle after N1. Single source of truth: Config.CYCLE_TARGETS + cycle_target(mode, cycles_done) helper; all five scattered sites (HP-activation banner, Normal check, HP check, cycle-2 announcement, status display) now read it; _c2_* dynamic stores removed. Day-cap on LOSSES (drawdown brake / C174 budget stop) is unaffected — capping losses and capping profits are different concerns and only the former survives."),
            ("C176", "Target-calculation fix-set from log_c175 (user-flagged; 8 trades 5W/3L +$0.07 — was ≈+$1.2 without the bugs). F1 PRICE-SPACE PLANNED TARGET: C49 floored the target at 1.2×PRU — a PnL-space unit (ATR×lev, capped 6.0) applied as a PRICE percent — so BEAT/BRETT/DEXE all printed the same phantom '+7.2%' and the C48 PLANNED_TARGET take-profit NEVER fired intraday (the per-position profit monetizer was dead; only peaks/session sweeps cashed out). Floor now = 1.5×ATR(entry), the same projective price-space unit Gate-4 uses. F2 SWEEP RACE PROTECTION: BEAT's +$0.15 win tripped the Cycle-2 target with 61s-old BRETT marked ≈flat; the sequential market-sweep filled BRETT 7s later into a -3.8% 1m flush (-$1.24, sweep net -$1.10) — and BRETT bounced +4.8% within 2min of the fill. 'Target achieved' sweeps now SPARE any position at ≤-0.3×PRU live (handed to normal exits/budget stop); banked result ≥ checked equity by construction. F3 VOLATILITY TRUTH: PRU cap 6→10 (BRETT true 7.94 was reported 25% calmer to every PRU consumer; C174 budget stop bounds $ regardless) + extreme-vol MARGIN scale: TR-ATR>2.5% → margin ×(2.5/ATR, floor 0.45) — C61 capped leverage but $16 on a ±5-10%/1m coin still lost $1.24/61s; $ per ATR-unit now ≈constant across pairs. F4 float display ('target 0.37520000000000153%' → .2f)."),
            ("C175", "Forensic fix-set from log_c174 (30min, 0 trades while 1h=-0.95 R=-0.53 impulse unfolded; N52 blocked 6-13/scan + late_leg 14-16/scan; chart truth: blocked shorts fell another 1.7-3.6% over 2h — HYPE -3.55%, DYDX -2.99%, ZK -2.97%, FET -2.90% = +5-10% PnL missed at 3x). F2 EXHAUSTION = DISTANCE × DECELERATION × AGE: caps built from the calm period are blown past by a fresh impulse within 2-3 candles — a leg printing full-size candles in its own direction is BURNING fuel, not out of it. Continuation blocked only when X beyond cap AND leg velocity <0.6 of its own mean (or last body flipped) AND leg age ≥3 settled candles; hot over-cap legs get a stretch tax (×0.88-0.93) instead. Engine exports age/vel/decel. Retro: tonight's impulse shorts now pass; BEAT#3 blow-off (decelerating after the 5.87 top) still blocked; BEAT#2 full-velocity winner returns. F3 late-leg: micro_exhaustion (candle-anatomy stretch detector) reads the impulse itself — when N52 says the leg is hot it cannot be the SOLE forward objection; a markov/CVD/wave objection must exist. F1 CANDLE ALIGNMENT (user audit): empirically PROVEN the bot reads settled Bitget-grid candles exactly as chart-watchers do (logged XLM N52 3.1/2.8/1.11 reproduced digit-for-digit from the settled series ending at the 17:15-open candle; forming-inclusive math does NOT match) — C151 wrapper covers every OHLCV path (1m/limit=3 live-feedback exempt by design). The one real defect: the 180s OHLCV cache TTL was boundary-blind, serving a series LACKING the just-settled candle for up to 3min after every :00/:15/:30/:45 — cache now valid only within the SAME 15m bucket."),
            ("C174", "Forensic fix-set from log_c173 ×2 (combined 2W/4L -$2.48; two catastrophic exits via SESSION brakes at -5.35%/-7.30% PnL — single trades consuming >100% of the $1.25 day cap). Market truth: from 11:57 UTC the whole board V-reversed +2-5% (BEAT +8.8%, EPIC +7.5%); the bot shorted APT at the final flush bottom and USELESS into the squeeze, then later longed BEAT a third time at its +22.6% blow-off top (RSI-82 brake + TF-tension + moved-penalty all fired, score still 1.003 — stacked signal penalties cannot tame euphoria they all read from). N52 RELATIVISTIC PRESSURE & EXHAUSTION ENGINE (user mandate): ATR-unit zigzag legs; LEG CAPACITY = pair's own p70 of completed leg travels (personal fuel tank); X = current travel/capacity; continuation entries blocked at X≥1.0, graduated penalty 0.8-1.0, mild bonus for fading X≥1.2 opposite legs; NEXT-CANDLE net-pressure forecast (signed body persistence damped by (1-X²) + effort-vs-result absorption) in ATR units → %, logged 🔮. True-range ATR computed in-engine (close-to-close _atr_proj understated USELESS at the 0.30% floor while it ranged 8.5%/day). F2 PER-TRADE BUDGET STOP: hard stop = tighter of (PRU-relativistic, half the REMAINING day budget) — USELESS would have cut at ≈-$0.45 not -$1.39, BEAT#3 at ≈-$0.63 not -$1.27. F3 1H REGIME-SHOCK: |Δ1h|≥0.60 between readings (USELESS trap: -0.88→+0.18 in 13min while R lagged at -0.41) → 30min guard blocking counter-shock entries + suspending stale-R trend unlocks when R opposes the shock. F4 VIOLENT-DRIFT ABORT: adverse signal→fill drift beyond 0.8×ATR (BEAT#3 -1.54%) aborts the entry instead of trimming margin 30%."),
            ("C173", "Forensic fix-set from log_c172 (2W/1L +$0.40, 67% WR — exits well-timed vs subsequent tape; the 14:48 R=-0.53 blocks correctly dodged the capitulation-flush bottom per chart verification). F1 PROJECTOR TIME-BASE INTEGRITY: _R_history appended on every call, mixing ~300s scan steps with 60s monitor refreshes — finite-difference velocity across inconsistent Δt flip-flopped strengthening↔exhausting within 76s at identical R (14:46/14:47), coin-flipping Step 3 unlocks per thread-write order, and printed a ±0.60 proj overshoot (R=-0.40→proj -1.00) that ×1.15-boosted the losing XLM entry. Fixed: ≥150s append-gating with in-place refresh, ±0.25 one-step swing clamp, 2-read hysteresis before state commits. F2 hp_vol_floor high-score override (score≥0.70 & vol≥$0.75M) — USELESS score 0.724 was blocked for hours solely by the absolute $1.5M floor (C123 documented the same wound: CGPT 1.176 blocked while +7%); downstream C172 timing gates still screen such candidates. F3/F5 COMPLETE pending-sweep: exhaustive audit found 15 more post-capture gates lacking reason-updates (hp_close_losers, h1_decay, corr_cap, heuristic, mtf_disagree, dir_proj_conflict, late_stage, range_noedge, taker_block, hp_counter_trend, low_eqi, micro_wave, vol_fading, exhaustion_hard, vol_floor) + hp_vol_floor + hp_weak_macro — all 20 now record real reasons; audited to zero unswept continues. F4 HP trend-ride: with-trend + |R|≥0.45 + strengthening waives the same-direction tax and caps compounded min_conf at 0.68 (was ~0.72 → low_confidence axed 14-18/29 per scan; HP took 1 trade in 3h35m vs Normal 2 in 57min)."),
            ("C172", "Forensic fix-set from log_c171 (2W/3L reported +$0.05, TRUE ≈ -$0.35; 24 consecutive starved scans during the second leg down). F1 Gate-4 projective target: with-trend breakdown/breakout target was distance-to-20-candle-extreme → 0.0% on every new-low short (poor_reward_risk=21/30 while ADA sat at RSI 15); now re-projected to 1.5×ATR when _trend_breakout (Gate-3 C163 condition) — Golden-Rule sweep completed. F2 forward-conflict timing gates (with-trend only): (a) ABSORPTION VETO — real_cvd ≥0.40 opposing + RSI stretched = other side loading at the extreme (SLX cvd=+0.57 @RSI28 → bounced, stopped, THEN fell -5.5%); (b) LATE-LEG check — room<10% of leg + a forward signal (markov/real_cvd/wavefunction/-micro_exhaustion) actively opposing (≤-0.25) with forward-mean<+0.05 (AR markov=+0.41, PENDLE micro_exh=-0.67). Retroactive: blocks all 3 losses, passes both HYPE wins → 2W/0L +$0.68 true. F3 HP exit NameError: min-hold check referenced _max_loss_pct 63 lines before definition → in HP mode every exit eval <25min crashed silently (no intelligent exits) — relocated below hard stop. F4 truthful exit accounting: PnL now computed from the ACTUAL fill price (order placed first); SLX booked -$0.19 vs real -$0.59. F5 nearest-miss reason=pending → real gate reason recorded at all five late gates incl. post_penalty_quality (live-verified: ALLO reason resolved). Plus: 2 C159-class unguarded dict iterations re-snapshotted (run_learning vs record_trade cross-thread race)."),
            ("C171", "Integration audit: fourier/markov/wavefunction were computed ONLY in dead full_analysis → NEVER live → absent from entry scoring AND read as 0 by the DRI exit calc. Same dead-end class as C140/C165/C169. Now computed in quick_scan (live) and added to _skill_keys; markov direction correctly derived from next_state (was wrong-key). calculus de-duplicated (already in base _calc_score). Decision vector now 48 signals; all named components verified live + projective."),
